# Management

This document is the capability router for repository governance tooling. It answers **which manager and command should be used for an operation**. It does not redefine the detailed policy owned by the linked governance document.

## Capability map

| Capability | Owner | Canonical command | Use when | Governing document |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Check initialization state | `initialization-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/initialization-manager.py status` | Determine whether the workspace is still a reusable starter or already a project. | `initialization.md` |
| Initialize project identity | `initialization-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/initialization-manager.py init --project <slug> --version vN.N.N` | Perform the one-time starter-to-project identity transition before project work. | `initialization.md` |
| Validate initialization | `initialization-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/initialization-manager.py validate` | Check synchronized identity/provenance after initialization. | `initialization.md` |
| Audit workspace | `workspace-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py audit` | Check completeness, transient-state hygiene, symlinks, and recovery-safe workspace structure. | `recovery.md` |
| Capture canonical pre-state | `workspace-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py pre --version vN.N.N` | Preserve the last complete source state immediately before work toward a greater target version. | `recovery.md` |
| Capture repeatable checkpoint | `workspace-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py capture --kind checkpoint --version vN.N.N` | Preserve an additional non-promoted state without colliding with the singleton `-pre` identity. | `recovery.md` |
| Verify promoted recovery | `workspace-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py verify --version vN.N.N` | Prove that snapshot, bundle, checksum, metadata, modes, cold extraction, and deterministic reproduction agree. | `recovery.md` |
| Verify canonical pre-state | `workspace-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py verify --version vN.N.N --pre` | Re-verify the predecessor capture for a target version. | `recovery.md` |
| Verify timestamped capture | `workspace-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py verify --version vN.N.N --kind checkpoint --timestamp YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ` | Re-verify one exact repeatable recovery identity. | `recovery.md` |
| Prune timestamped captures | `workspace-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py cleanup --version vN.N.N --kind checkpoint --retain 3` | Remove older verified captures while retaining the newest requested count. | `recovery.md` |
| Seal promoted recovery | `workspace-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py seal --version vN.N.N` | Produce and verify the promoted recovery state; matching verified `-pre` artifacts are cleaned after success. | `recovery.md` |
| Seal while retaining pre-state | `workspace-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py seal --version vN.N.N --keep-pre` | Promote a recovery state while intentionally preserving its matching predecessor capture. | `recovery.md` |
| Create iteration ledger | `iteration-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/iteration-manager.py create <slug> vN.N.N --base HEAD` | Start a governed transition record with `manifest.yaml` and `change.md`. | `iteration.md` |
| Render bounded changelog | `iteration-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/iteration-manager.py changelog <slug> vN.N.N` | Regenerate the root latest-20 changelog view from iteration change records. | `iteration.md` |
| Seal iteration transition | `iteration-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/iteration-manager.py seal <slug> vN.N.N --result HEAD` | Generate and certify the reconstructable `changes.diff` for committed base/result states. | `iteration.md` |
| Verify iteration transition | `iteration-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/iteration-manager.py verify <slug> vN.N.N` | Prove that the recorded base plus diff reconstructs the recorded result projection. | `iteration.md` |
| Validate iteration ledger | `iteration-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/iteration-manager.py validate` | Check all iteration directories and manifests structurally. | `iteration.md` |
| Allocate governed record ID | `record-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/record-manager.py next-id <type>` | Determine the next stable ID for a managed record family. | `artifacts.md` |
| Create governed record | `record-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/record-manager.py create <type> "<title>"` | Create a durable decision/evidence/roadmap-style artifact from its template. | `artifacts.md` |
| Allocate knowledge ID | `knowledge-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/knowledge-manager.py next-id` | Determine the next stable `NOTE-XXXX` identity. | `artifacts.md` |
| Create knowledge note | `knowledge-manager.py` | `python3 agents/scripts/knowledge-manager.py create <topic> "<title>"` | Preserve reusable researched or synthesized knowledge with provenance. | `artifacts.md` |

## Manager boundaries

### Initialization manager

Owns the one-time **starter → project identity** transition. It updates only declared identity/history surfaces, preserves starter provenance, and refuses to initialize an already initialized project. It does not perform global text replacement or rename the workspace directory.

### Workspace manager

Owns complete recoverable **workspace states** and their external recovery artifacts. It audits, captures, verifies, prunes timestamped captures, and seals states. It does not own Git transition history or governed record acceptance.

### Iteration manager

Owns reconstructable **transitions** between committed Git states. It creates iteration ledgers, renders the bounded changelog, generates diffs, and verifies replay. It does not promote recovery snapshots.

### Record manager

Owns stable identities and mechanical creation/validation for governed record families. It does not decide that a record is accepted merely because it can render or validate it.

### Knowledge manager

Owns stable knowledge-note identities and mechanical creation/validation. It does not turn example knowledge namespaces into project authority.

## Routing rule

Use the manager that owns the **artifact or state transition being manipulated**, then follow the linked governance document for policy details. `management.md` is an operational index; if its summary conflicts with `recovery.md`, `iteration.md`, or `artifacts.md`, the specific governance document wins.
</file>

