# Coordination

| ID | Topic | Summary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `CORD-0001` | Ownership | Give each authoritative mutable transition a clear owner. |
| `CORD-0002` | Idempotency | Define duplicate behavior for operations that can be retried or redelivered. |
| `CORD-0003` | Ordering | Document ordering, lock, lease, and transaction assumptions when correctness depends on them. |
| `CORD-0004` | Recovery | Specify how partial progress is reconciled after interruption. |


## CORD-0001 - Ownership

Avoid multiple components independently deciding the same authoritative state. Shared mutable workflows should identify which component owns each transition and which participants only request, observe, or reconcile it.

## CORD-0002 - Idempotency

Where effects may be attempted more than once, define the idempotency key or duplicate policy, what counts as the same operation, what evidence is returned on replay, and which effects are safe to repeat.

## CORD-0003 - Ordering

Specify lock or lease ownership and expiry, transaction boundaries, sequencing guarantees, queue ordering, or compare-and-swap behavior only where they are required. Do not imply stronger ordering than the underlying system can provide.

## CORD-0004 - Recovery

Define retry and backoff behavior, cancellation, crash recovery, stale ownership handling, and reconciliation after partial failure. Recovery should preserve authoritative invariants rather than merely rerun every step blindly.
</file>

