# Guide Index

| ID | Topic | Summary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GUID-0001` | Scope | Define the role and authority of repository guides. |
| `GUID-0002` | Registry | Register the fixed guide set and semantic content-ID prefixes. |
| `GUID-0003` | Identity | Define how guide content receives stable cross-reference IDs. |
| `GUID-0004` | Classification | Use conventions only when the final guide scope is unresolved. |


## GUID-0001 - Scope

`agents/guides/` contains current repository engineering guidance organized by known scope. A guide is the normal destination for a durable rule once its subject is clear. Guides are subordinate to repository governance and accepted decision or constraint records, but they should be the easiest place to discover the current engineering expectation.

## GUID-0002 - Registry

The starter uses a fixed guide set with stable semantic prefixes. The prefix is part of the cross-reference contract and MUST NOT be changed after an ID has been issued. New guide domains require an explicit governance change rather than ad hoc file creation.

| Guide | Prefix | Scope |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `architecture.md` | `ARCH` | architecture ownership, layers, dependency direction, authority |
| `topology.md` | `TOPO` | repository, package, service, process, and dependency shape |
| `boundaries.md` | `BNDR` | ownership, dependency, adapter, and cross-layer boundaries |
| `flow.md` | `FLOW` | data movement, lineage, transformation, and rebuildability |
| `workflows.md` | `WKFL` | behavior spanning components, effects, and state transitions |
| `storage.md` | `STOR` | durable stores, retention, backup, and recovery |
| `persistence.md` | `PERS` | durable representation, migrations, serialization, and lifecycle |
| `configuration.md` | `CONF` | configuration, secrets, precedence, and validation |
| `coordination.md` | `CORD` | shared state, concurrency, ordering, idempotency, and recovery |
| `security.md` | `SECU` | trust boundaries, access, secrets, and sensitive evidence |
| `observability.md` | `OBSV` | logs, metrics, traces, health, and correlation |
| `testing.md` | `TEST` | behavioral verification, fixtures, integration, and recovery gates |
| `portability.md` | `PORT` | cross-language/platform boundaries and implementation replacement |
| `naming.md` | `NAME` | repository naming rules and identity distinctions |
| `terminology.md` | `TERM` | canonical vocabulary and external/internal term mapping |
| `api.md` | `API` | stable public interfaces, compatibility, errors, and effect semantics |

## GUID-0003 - Identity

Every top-level guide declares a semantic prefix in YAML frontmatter. The opening index allocates `{PREFIX}-NNNN` IDs to durable content units, and each indexed ID has exactly one matching expanded section. IDs are append-only identities: do not renumber or reuse them because prose moves, a heading changes, or an entry is retired. If a rule is superseded, preserve the ID and record the new authority in the section.

## GUID-0004 - Classification

`agents/guides/conventions/` is a classification inbox, not another guide taxonomy. If the correct destination is known, write or promote the rule directly into the matching top-level guide. Create `CONVENTION-XXXX` only while durable rule scope is genuinely unresolved. See `agents/governance/artifacts.md` for the complete artifact-routing model.
</file>

