# Security

| ID | Topic | Summary |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SECU-0001` | Secrets | Keep secret material out of ordinary source, logs, bundles, and errors. |
| `SECU-0002` | Trust | Authenticate and authorize at the boundary that owns the protected capability. |
| `SECU-0003` | Bounds | Bound attacker-controlled work and dangerous interpretation. |
| `SECU-0004` | Identity | Do not confuse temporary credentials or signed locators with durable identity. |
| `SECU-0005` | Watch data boundary | Network observation is explicit, local-first, and payload-minimized by default. |


## SECU-0001 - Secrets

Credentials, tokens, private keys, sensitive headers, and equivalent values must not be committed to source control, copied into normal logs, included in generated release bundles, or returned through user-visible errors. Sanitization applies to durable evidence as well as runtime output.

## SECU-0002 - Trust

Treat external input as untrusted until validated. Authenticate before processing sensitive or expensive payloads when possible, and authorize the requested capability at the boundary that owns it rather than relying on downstream assumptions.

## SECU-0003 - Bounds

Constrain input sizes, timeouts, redirects, recursion, archive extraction, path resolution, decompression, parsing depth, and other resource consumption where relevant. Prefer safe defaults and explicit rejection over unbounded best effort.

## SECU-0004 - Identity

Signed URLs, session tokens, bearer credentials, temporary handles, and similar security-sensitive locators should not be persisted or exposed as stable project identity unless the external contract explicitly makes them durable.


## SECU-0005 - Watch data boundary

For `crsniffer`, network observation is a user-mediated capability rather than ambient background collection. The baseline must collect only while an explicit Watch is active for its target tab, remain local-first, and exclude bodies, form payloads, credential-bearing headers, cookies, and WebSocket/EventSource message payloads. Service-worker restart may reconcile active application intent, but browser/profile restart must not silently resume Watch. Page-derived values are a separately governed input and remain untrusted until validated. `CONSTRAINT-0003` is the normative floor; later implementation ADRs may refine mechanisms but must not silently weaken it.
</file>

