# ADR-0002 - Immutable Resource Pipeline and Declarative Packagizer

## Decision summary

Raw network facts remain immutable ResourceObservations. Classification, duplicate folding, admission filtering and Packagizer actions are explicit derived/evaluation layers. Watch start freezes the effective filters/rules/templates, and Preview/Test uses the same evaluator contract as live processing.

## Decision

- Raw identity is WatchSession plus Chrome request identity; redirect/auth stages remain one logical observation while a new request ID is a new raw occurrence.
- User-facing duplicate folding is reversible and never deletes occurrence provenance.
- Semantic resource kinds are `image`, `video`, `stream_manifest`, `audio`, `other`, `unknown`; MIME/type/path evidence and classification reason are retained separately.
- Images selects semantic images. Videos selects semantic video plus recognized HLS/DASH stream manifests.
- Admission is `(selected type preset OR include glob) AND NOT exclude glob`; exclusions are final vetoes and normal persisted history begins at admission.
- Resource glob v1 is full canonical URL without fragment, query retained, case-sensitive full-string matching with only `*`, `?` and explicit escapes.
- Packagizer rules are ordered; conditions in one rule are ANDed and read immutable source context. Actions update a derived projection only. `stop_processing` applies after a successful matched rule.
- Missing is distinct from empty/null/false/zero. Templates use namespaced source tokens and a bounded safe transform registry; arbitrary JS/eval and sensitive credential/body/raw-payload tokens are rejected.
- A matched rule's action set is atomic on template/evaluation failure.
- Preview/Test and live processing share the same pure semantic engine and produce structural/redacted diagnostics by default.

## Deferred/later scope

Regex conditions/transforms, rule import/export file format, historical bulk re-evaluation, downloader control, arbitrary plugins/scripts and sensitive token families are outside the baseline unless separately governed.

## Validation and evidence

CONSTRAINT-0004; MATRIX-0005 through MATRIX-0007; FINDING-0011 through FINDING-0016.
</file>

