# ADR-0003 - Exact-Document PageContext and Declarative Page Field Mapping

## Decision summary

Page enrichment is a separate exact-document authority layer. A PageContext is bound to WatchSession + tab + top-level document identity + same-document revision. Page fields evaluate on demand against the exact target document in an isolated scripting world and fail closed when attribution is stale or ambiguous.

## Decision

- Chrome `documentId` is the hard cross-document stale boundary. Same-document History/fragment transitions advance/invalidate through `pageRevision` even when documentId is unchanged.
- Resource observations retain initiating/top-document attribution evidence; current-tab state must not substitute for ambiguous historical attribution.
- Exact-document evaluation targets the accepted top document and verifies returned identity before consumption.
- CSS node results normalize to ordered static node arrays. XPath preserves typed scalar results and ordered snapshots for node results.
- Baseline read modes are text content, rendered inner text, named attribute, direct primitive named property, and raw typed XPath scalar.
- Cardinality is explicit (`first`, `optional_one`, `exact_one`, `many`). Missing remains distinct from falsey values.
- Fallback occurs only on Missing or explicit candidate rejection; evaluation/read/cardinality/transform/validation errors do not silently fall through.
- Reusable PageFieldMappings are declarative, revisioned definitions. Watch freezes only mappings referenced by its enabled frozen rules/templates.
- `${page.*}` and `${field.<slug>}` are immutable source tokens with exact-context provenance. Stale/unavailable/unattributed values become Missing.

## Negative scope

Continuous ambient MutationObserver scraping, arbitrary page JS/eval, dotted arbitrary property traversal, automatic markup capture, and baseline subframe mapping UI are excluded.

## Validation and evidence

CONSTRAINT-0005; MATRIX-0008 through MATRIX-0010; FINDING-0017 through FINDING-0022.
</file>

