# ADR-0004 - MV3 Runtime, Local Persistence, and Versioned State Authority

## Decision summary

The implementation family is Chrome Manifest V3 with Chrome 116+ as the initial browser denominator, WXT, Vue 3, TypeScript and a Side Panel. Privileged background/service-worker code coordinates Watch, capture, evaluation and persistence. Durable domain/history authority is local IndexedDB; browser-lifetime active coordination uses `chrome.storage.session`; small preferences/install metadata use `chrome.storage.local`.

## Decision

- Exact WXT/Vue/TypeScript/Node/package-manager versions are not inherited from research; ROADMAP-0002 STEP-01 must fresh-check and lock exact versions reproducibly.
- Service-worker globals and open Ports are caches/transport only, never canonical state.
- Side Panel state is a reconstructable presentation/query/command projection.
- IndexedDB owns revisioned reusable definitions, immutable WatchSession history, admitted ResourceObservations and any durable enrichment/projection/meta records required by the accepted model.
- Exact physical IndexedDB v1 store/index topology is deliberately a ROADMAP-0002 implementation decision, but logical authorities must remain distinguishable rather than one opaque untyped blob.
- Physical DB version and per-object logical schema version are distinct. Structural upgrades are bounded; long logical migration is resumable after open.
- Reusable definitions carry stable IDs/revisions. Frozen WatchSession composition records exact effective revisions/digests so later edits do not reinterpret historical evaluation.
- Cross-context messages use a versioned JSON-safe envelope with explicit request/session/tab/document context and typed result/error semantics.
- Retention is bounded/configurable/disclosed; Clear is user-visible. Quota/write failure enters degraded/error state rather than silently losing admitted history.
- `storage.sync`, baseline `unlimitedStorage`, remote telemetry/upload and silent browser-restart Watch resume are rejected for canonical history/coordination.

## Validation and evidence

CONSTRAINT-0006; MATRIX-0011/0012; FINDING-0023 through FINDING-0026; FINDING-0031; REFERENCE-0013.
</file>

