# ADR-0005 - Watch-First Side Panel Information Architecture and UI Recovery

## Decision summary

The primary UI is a narrow Side Panel with three task-level destinations: **Watch**, **Rules**, and **Settings**. Watch is the default and primary CTA. Advanced filters, Packagizer details, Token Browser, Page Fields, permissions and diagnostics are progressively disclosed in context rather than promoted into many top-level modes.

## Decision

- Watch contains exact tab/page scope, Watch/Stop, readiness/permission status, Images/Videos, advanced include/exclude globs, live resource stream and selected-resource detail.
- Rules contains ordered Packagizer rules/templates, Token Browser, Preview/Test and referenced Page Field dependencies.
- Settings contains retention/Clear, privacy/support/diagnostics and small preferences. PageField mapping management may be reached contextually from Rules and Settings without becoming a mandatory top-level tab.
- Side Panel opens/reconnects by querying durable/background authority; messaging can provide append deltas but cannot be correctness authority.
- Large resource streams use bounded hydration, append-only deltas, stable row identity, windowing/virtualization and shallow immutable presentation data. Exact library/thresholds are implementation evidence.
- Primary controls use semantic/native HTML where practical, are keyboard complete, have visible/non-color-only focus and state, respect reduced motion, externalize strings from the first implementation, and target WCAG 2.2 AA-oriented reflow/focus/status behavior.
- Persistent diagnostics are structural/redacted by default and do not retain raw URL/page-field/token values unless a deliberate user-facing workflow requires them.

## Consequences

The UI reflects task hierarchy rather than internal domain count and can survive panel/service-worker churn without inventing a second state store.

## Validation and evidence

CONSTRAINT-0006; MATRIX-0013; FINDING-0027 through FINDING-0029; current Vue/WXT/Chrome accessibility refresh in REFERENCE-0013.
</file>

