# AUDIT-0002 - v0.0.1 ROADMAP-0001 STEP-01 Research Completion

## Objective

Assess whether STEP-01 has enough current source-backed evidence to hand network-observation, permission, Watch lifecycle, security/privacy, and data-boundary assumptions to later research without beginning extension implementation.

## Scope

Current Chrome MV3 network observation/permissions/debugger/navigation/service-worker/messaging authority, W3C Resource Timing, Cat Catch 2.7.2 product evidence, freshly frozen crscraper v0.0.36 governance donor, ROADMAP-0001 STEP-01 records, and absence of production runtime code.

## Method

- Perform a fresh Library donor check before mutation and freeze crscraper v0.0.36 as immutable evidence.
- Refresh current first-party Chrome documentation for `webRequest`, `activeTab`, `permissions`, `debugger`, CDP Network, service-worker lifecycle, `webNavigation`, messaging and Web Store Limited Use.
- Compare current W3C Resource Timing and Cat Catch product behavior/permission posture.
- Separate source facts from repository interpretation in research-data, findings and two qualitative matrices.
- Inspect changed-file scope for research-only compliance; donor code is not executed, imported, built, tested, benchmarked or certified.

## Evidence

REFERENCE-0002 revision 2; REFERENCE-0004 revision 2; REFERENCE-0006; FINDING-0006 through FINDING-0010; MATRIX-0003; MATRIX-0004; CONSTRAINT-0003; STEP-01 research-data capture; exact crscraper v0.0.36 archive/hash.

## Findings

| Finding | Severity | Evidence | Recommendation |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Comprehensive passive third-party resource visibility requires broader host authority than `activeTab` provides | high | FINDING-0006, MATRIX-0003 | carry optional broad HTTP(S) host grant from Watch as preferred baseline candidate |
| debugger/CDP has disproportionate permission, sensitivity and target-lifecycle cost for baseline Watch | high | FINDING-0007, MATRIX-0003 | defer to separately justified advanced mode rather than baseline |
| Resource Timing/DOM cannot serve as canonical request authority | medium | FINDING-0008 | keep as supplemental page evidence only |
| Watch must survive service-worker restart through durable application intent, not globals | high | FINDING-0009, MATRIX-0004 | hand durable session/persistence questions to STEP-02/04 |
| Baseline network observation can meet product intent without bodies/credentials/message payloads | high | FINDING-0010, CONSTRAINT-0003 | enforce local-first metadata-minimized baseline |
| `webRequest` has documented visibility gaps, including renderer in-memory cache | medium | MATRIX-0003 | do not market or design baseline as mathematically complete capture |

## Interpretation

STEP-01 resolves the key research question strongly enough to continue: `webRequest` with explicit user-mediated optional host authority is the preferred baseline candidate, but it remains a research disposition rather than an implementation ADR. The Watch/session and privacy boundaries are sufficiently explicit for STEP-02 to define resource/rule semantics without coupling them to service-worker memory or debugger-only data.

## Recommendations

- Mark ROADMAP-0001 STEP-01 complete in v0.0.1.
- Authorize only **v0.0.2 / STEP-02** next.
- Keep debugger/CDP, exact persistence technology, final UI permission flow, XPath page-field semantics, and final architecture decisions in their assigned later steps.
- Do not add production extension code during Wave 1.

## Unresolved questions

All STEP-02 through STEP-05 questions remain intentionally open, including exact resource identity/dedup, glob/rule/token grammar, page-field mapping, persistence/UI stack and final ADR synthesis.

## Closure / follow-up

This audit closes STEP-01 when managed records, roadmap cross-references, research-only changed-file scope, iteration ledger/replay and recovery sealing validate. Next authorized work is v0.0.2 / ROADMAP-0001 STEP-02 only.

