# AUDIT-0003 - v0.0.2 ROADMAP-0001 STEP-02 Research Completion

## Objective

Assess whether STEP-02 defines deterministic resource observation, classification/dedup, type/glob admission, Packagizer rule/token/template and Preview semantics strongly enough for STEP-03 page-field enrichment research without beginning extension implementation.

## Scope and method

- Recheck the latest crscraper governance donor before mutation; v0.0.36 remains latest and is reused by exact frozen identity rather than duplicated.
- Refresh current Chrome request-identity/ResourceType/glob/match-pattern authority, WHATWG URL/MIME standards, IANA HLS/DASH media-type authority, JDownloader Packagizer behavior and Cat Catch 2.7.2 filter/token/preview evidence.
- Separate source facts from crsniffer interpretation in research-data and findings.
- Compare resource identity/classification/dedup, filter/glob, and Packagizer/token/preview scenarios in three matrices.
- Inspect changed-file scope for research-only compliance. No donor code or product runtime is executed, imported, built, tested, benchmarked or probed.

## Findings

| Area | Accepted STEP-02 research disposition |
| --- | --- |
| Raw identity | one immutable `ResourceObservation` per WatchSession + Chrome requestId logical trace; URL dedup is separate/reversible |
| Classification | retain independent MIME/Chrome-type/extension evidence and explicit `unknown`; generic Chrome `media` is not video |
| Defaults | Images=`image`; Videos=`video` + `stream_manifest` |
| Globs | dedicated whole-canonical-URL v1 grammar with `*`, `?`, explicit escaping, case-sensitive full-string match; exclude veto |
| Admission | `(selected type OR include glob) AND NOT exclude glob`; no positive lane admits nothing |
| Rules | ordered, declarative, frozen per WatchSession, immutable source context, actions write derived projection only |
| Tokens | namespaced `${resource.*}`/`${watch.*}`, explicit Missing sentinel, safe transform allowlist; reserve page/field namespaces for STEP-03 |
| Upstream syntax | adapt JDownloader/Cat Catch experience; reject exact `<jd:...>`, environment/plugin/raw-cookie/payload token inheritance |
| Preview | same pure evaluator as live; structural persisted explanation without raw values by default |

## Pre-change recovery note

The first automatically named `v0.0.2-pre` capture was produced from the clean Git tree after `git clean -fd`; Git cannot retain three empty governed directories (`agents/records/adrs`, `deferrals`, `issues`), so that capture has the same 121 files but 31 rather than 34 directories. It is preserved as immutable evidence and is not rewritten.

Before semantic STEP-02 changes, those three directories were restored from the promoted v0.0.1 snapshot and a separately named predecessor-reference recovery capture was created. Its tree SHA-256 is exactly `a934decfbf3352999962f288b266ad0459f243ecd08f2be205d721ac2eac8bb4`, matching the promoted v0.0.1 predecessor. The discrepancy is directory-only; no predecessor file bytes drifted.

## Acceptance assessment

STEP-02 satisfies all roadmap work items and acceptance evidence. The product floor now has explicit, future-testable contracts for Images/Videos, custom glob filtering, resource identity/dedup, ordered Packagizer-like rules, namespaced templates/missing values, and Preview explanation. CONSTRAINT-0004 prevents later implementation from weakening raw-history immutability or silently turning rule evaluation into executable/user-code behavior.

No final architecture ADR is created: STEP-05 remains the authority that accepts/supersedes research candidates after STEP-03/04 evidence exists.

