# AUDIT-0009 — v0.0.21 ROADMAP-0003 STEP-03 Virtualized Resource History UX

## Audit objective

Determine whether STEP-03 turns existing durable Watch/resource authority into a bounded, reconnect-safe, virtualized result/detail experience without adding a second canonical history model or pulling STEP-04+ UI domains forward.

## Accepted implementation

- `IndexedDbResourceHistoryReader` queries the existing `watchSessions.byCreatedAt` and `resourceObservations.byWatchSessionObservedAt` indexes with bounded cursors; older-page continuation seeks the exact key/primary-key position instead of restarting from newest.
- `ResourceHistoryService` projects recent human Watch-session summaries, bounded newest-first resource pages and one selected-resource detail over immutable stored authority.
- Primary rows include admitted projected/failed occurrences; rejected observations remain outside the primary results surface rather than being reinterpreted as results.
- Same canonical URL occurrences remain separate stable rows; STEP-03 does not destructively collapse occurrence provenance.
- Search is bounded to URL/filename/group; kind/status filters are bounded query predicates. Arbitrary grouping/sort is deliberately not offered because accepted query/index authority does not justify it in this step.
- Side Panel rows use a shallow bounded buffer and fixed-row virtual window. Append invalidation re-queries a bounded newest page and merges by stable observation identity while preserving an existing selected item when still present.
- Watch history/session selection is human-facing (setup name/start time/live context); ordinary inspection never requires typing or copying a WatchSession ID.
- Selected detail presents source/response facts, derived filename/group/comment, page-enrichment status and structural explanation. Raw headers/body/cookies/credentials, request/document IDs and internal rule IDs are excluded from the normal detail contract.
- Control-plane schema remains v2. Additive one-shot `panel.resources.sessions`, `panel.resources.page` and `panel.resources.detail` operations each use independent freshness sequencing; Port messages remain invalidation-only.
- Live additions are summarized through passive status text instead of announcing every row.

## Scope fences confirmed

- No physical IndexedDB version/store/index change.
- No Chrome permission change.
- No resource Port becomes canonical streaming state.
- No Rules/Templates editor, Token Browser, Preview/Test, Page Field editor/assist, Settings/retention/Clear workflow or reusable-definition lifecycle work from STEP-04+.
- No final capacity threshold is claimed: current page/scan/buffer values remain tunable implementation constants under STEP-12 performance authority.

## Repository-controlled validation

- Available TypeScript 5.8.3 compiles all 11 repository project configurations.
- Complete repository-controlled product suite: 140/140 tests pass.
- Focused persistence: 7/7; resources: 15/15; control-plane/Side Panel source contract: 14/14.
- Resource tests cover bounded continuation/filtering, rejection exclusion, detail redaction and a 10,000-item virtual-window model that mounts only the visible+overscan window.
- Control-plane tests cover strict new operations and independent stale resource-page rejection.
- Persistence source contract verifies index/cursor/`continuePrimaryKey` use, no `getAll`, physical DB version 1 and unchanged store topology.

## Environment-only lanes

The selected Vue/WXT/vue-tsc dependencies are not hydrated in this recovery environment; native Vue SFC typecheck, WXT build/package, packaged Chrome and assistive-technology execution remain `deferred_environment` and are not counted as passes. Repository-controlled TypeScript/domain/source contracts are the STEP-03 executable evidence available here.

