# AUDIT-0010 — v0.0.24 ROADMAP-0003 STEP-06 Structured Page Field and Exact-Page Assist

## Audit objective

Determine whether STEP-06 makes the accepted PageFieldMapping capability fully authorable/testable through structured controls and bounded exact-page helpers without weakening exact-document stale rejection, widening Chrome permissions, adding ambient page observation or pulling STEP-07+ product scope forward.

## Accepted implementation

- Added `PageFieldWorkspaceService` plus strict lowercase one-shot message/client operations over the existing `pageFieldMapping` definition catalog; no new store, physical IndexedDB version or durable authoring history is introduced.
- Structured working copies cover name/slug/enablement/required state; CSS/XPath selectors; XPath namespaces; ordered primary/fallback candidates; read mode/name; cardinality; rejection semantics; ordered transforms; typed fallback values; and final type/length/nonblank validation.
- Save as/Update are explicit and revision-fenced. Enabled slugs remain unique; stale conflicts preserve the local working copy. Historical/active WatchSessions remain immutable.
- `PageFieldEvaluationService.evaluateBody` exposes the existing pure mapping evaluator for transient authoring Test without creating a PageFieldSnapshot or replacing runtime semantics.
- Test reports bounded per-candidate match count/result kind/sample/error plus final value/Missing/error outcome; it re-checks the exact PageContext before/after candidate inspection and evaluation.
- Highlight and Pick use `chrome.scripting.executeScript` against the exact current `documentId` in explicit `ISOLATED` world. Returned document identity is checked before use.
- Pick is one-shot and helper output remains editable working-copy selector text. Manual CSS/XPath is equal authority and remains available without page assist.
- Highlight/pick overlays are temporary and best-effort cleared/cancelled by explicit Clear/Escape, hidden document/pagehide, PageContext navigation/revision replacement, Side Panel active-tab change, tab removal and permission loss. A stale result is rejected instead of applied to a replacement page.
- Runtime routing treats only Page Field save as a mutation invalidation; Test/Highlight/Pick/Clear are read-only query/assist operations.

## Permission/security review

- Existing permissions remain `storage`, `webRequest`, `webNavigation`, `scripting` plus optional HTTP/HTTPS host origins; STEP-06 adds no `activeTab`, `tabs`, required/broader host, debugger/CDP or MAIN-world authority.
- No MutationObserver, always-on content script, arbitrary user JavaScript/eval, body/header/cookie/credential capture or markup serialization is introduced.
- Assistance is explicit, bounded and fail-closed when host/document authority is unavailable or stale.

## Scope fences confirmed

- No generic STEP-07 Duplicate/Delete/import/export lifecycle for Page Fields.
- No Settings/retention/Clear/product-preference workflow.
- No change to WatchSession, ResourceObservation, PageFieldSnapshot, Packagizer, PageContext identity or persistence semantics beyond exposing the existing evaluation path for non-persisting Test.
- No new public file/import format and no scraper-specific Setup/Traversal concepts.

## Repository-controlled validation

- All 11 repository TypeScript project configurations compile with the available compiler.
- Complete repository-controlled product suite: **159/159 tests pass**.
- Focused Page Fields: **27/27**; PageContext: **11/11**; control-plane/Side Panel source contract: **14/14**.
- New tests cover exact-context Test/Highlight/Pick facts, stale-action rejection, lowercase message correlation, closure-free injected functions, full structured draft round-trip and pre-navigation/stop assist cleanup against the old exact document.
- `git diff --check` passes before governance sealing.

## Environment-only lanes

Native selected `vue-tsc`, WXT build/package, packaged Chrome and assistive-technology execution remain `deferred_environment` because the portable recovery environment does not contain hydrated selected dependencies. Repository-controlled source/domain contracts are the executable STEP-06 evidence available here; deferred lanes are not counted as passes.

