- `incognito: not_allowed` is explicit. The extension does not claim a certified private-browsing persistence model.
- Extension-page CSP is explicitly self-only; no remote executable code or arbitrary eval authority is introduced.
- Privileged runtime messages and Ports are authenticated to the current packaged extension ID/origin before reaching strict control-plane routers; untrusted Ports are disconnected.
- Existing strict message schemas/allowlists/revision checks remain the malformed-input boundary. No external message/Port handlers are added.
- Page Field assistance remains exact-document and isolated-world; permission state cannot substitute for current PageContext document/revision trust.
- HTTP(S) URL userinfo is removed before pending/durable observation state while path/query resource identity is preserved. Non-HTTP(S) observed/redirect URLs retain only scheme, preventing `data:` payload text from entering local history.
- Existing response payload minimization remains: raw request/response headers, cookies, bodies, credentials and secret-bearing values are not added to durable observation detail or normal diagnostics.
- Settings privacy copy now exposes same-extension privileged messaging, Incognito exclusion and self-only CSP as user-facing product behavior.

