# AUDIT-0014 — v0.0.30 ROADMAP-0003 STEP-12 Performance Capacity Accessibility Localization and Failure-Recovery Hardening

## Audit objective

Determine whether the feature-complete Crsniffer product remains bounded, accessible, localized and recoverable under representative large-history, burst, reconnect, retention-pressure and repeated storage-failure workloads, without inventing unsupported hard limits or pulling package/release work forward.

## Accepted implementation

- Resource history remains bounded and index/cursor-driven; no whole-history presentation hydration or deep canonical UI cache is introduced.
- Current page/scan/buffer constants remain unchanged because measured repository workloads do not justify tuning them. They are not reclassified as product maxima.
- New `ControlPlaneInvalidationBatcher` coalesces Port hint bursts into one 50ms presentation refresh wave. The Port remains latency-only; one-shot queries and stale-response rejection remain correctness authority.
- Virtualized dynamic resources preserve focusable/labelled list semantics, selected-row state, one summarized live region, 320px reflow, visible focus and reduced-motion behavior.
- Repeated observation write failure/replay remains idempotent and produces no duplicate canonical observations.
- Retention-pressure and reconnect-soak evidence exercises the real production selection/reconnect logic without widening deletion or presentation ownership.
- Failure/privacy contracts from STEP-10/11 remain intact; the hardening harness does not expose sensitive payloads in normal failure messages/evidence.

## Repository-controlled performance evidence

One recorded v0.0.30 run under Node 22.16.0 used `performance.now()` and passed every deliberately generous regression budget: 10k history scan, 10k merge burst, 100k virtual-window traversal, 10k invalidation hints, 5k-session retention pressure and 100 reconnect cycles. These timings are local regression evidence only (`portableTimingClaim=false`) and are not SLA/device claims.

## Browser/environment evidence

The origin-backed Chromium IndexedDB harness reached Chromium 144.0.7559.96 but the current headless/CDP context denied IndexedDB access. This lane is recorded `deferred_environment`. The selected WXT/vue-tsc package environment is still not hydrated, so generated extension-host performance, package install/upgrade and real assistive-technology/browser-package certification remain STEP-13/14 evidence, not STEP-12 passes.

## Donor disposition

Latest promoted Crscraper v0.0.54 remains the read-only donor. Its performance-readiness claim boundary and representative-capacity pattern are adapted; scraper-specific Run/scheduler/export/artifact-pruning semantics are not copied.

## Scope fence

No dependency hydration/lockfile work, generated WXT package certification, install/upgrade/store-readiness or final release-candidate user-story closure is introduced in v0.0.30.

## Conclusion

STEP-12 is accepted at the repository-controlled hardening level, subject to exact final candidate and cold-artifact revalidation. Phase P5 closes; only v0.0.31 / STEP-13 is authorized next.

## Revision history

