# AUDIT-0015 — v0.0.31 ROADMAP-0003 STEP-13 Build Package Install Upgrade and Store Readiness

## Audit objective

Determine whether Crsniffer can close STEP-13 with truthful repository-side release evidence while selected dependency/WXT/generated-extension/Web Store lanes are unavailable, and whether the Side Panel can become more Chrome-native-aware without changing its accepted general structure.

## Accepted repository implementation

- `scripts/check-release-readiness.mjs` fails on repository-owned package/manifest/migration/docs/theme defects but reports unavailable selected WXT/install/update/Web Store lanes as `deferred_environment`.
- Package/development dependency versions remain exact; no synthetic lockfile is created with the wrong npm/tool environment.
- Manifest permission/CSP/incognito/i18n authority remains unchanged from STEP-11.
- Existing persistence/settings tests remain the upgrade-semantic authority; no new data schema or reinterpretation is introduced.
- Store single-purpose/privacy/permission/support disclosure is reconciled in `docs/release/store-readiness.md`.
- Side Panel CSS gains a public-platform native-aware token layer using system colors and native control accent/contrast behavior while keeping Watch / Rules / Settings DOM/layout authority unchanged.
- Exact arbitrary Chrome custom-theme hue matching is explicitly not claimed; private Chrome WebUI/theme-token imitation is rejected.

## Environment disposition

The current environment lacks the declared npm 11.17.0 selected package installation, `package-lock.json`, `node_modules`, WXT/vue-tsc executables and generated `.wxt/tsconfig.json`. Native WXT build/package, generated manifest inspection, extension-origin install/update and Web Store submission are `deferred_environment`, non-blocking under normative repository governance.

The globally available npm/TypeScript binaries are not substituted as if they were the selected package toolchain.

## Release acceptance boundary

v0.0.31 may promote when repository release checks, full standalone TypeScript/product tests, managed-record validation, workspace audit, deterministic recovery seal and cold revalidation pass. Environment-only lanes remain explicit in the release report and are revisited later in a capable environment.

STEP-14 realistic final user stories/public promotion decision remain out of scope.

## Conclusion

