# CONSTRAINT-0001 - Wave 1 Research-Only Boundary

## Constraint

ROADMAP-0001 STEP-01 through STEP-05 are documentation/evidence iterations. They MUST NOT add production extension/runtime code, extension entrypoints, WXT/runtime configuration, executable product tests, browser probes, benchmarks, or schema prototypes. `src/` and production extension entrypoints remain absent until a separately governed successor roadmap authorizes implementation.

## Rationale / source

The current crscraper research-first workflow deliberately separates evidence accumulation, synthesis, and successor-roadmap creation from implementation. Freezing network-capture, permission, token, page-mapping, persistence, or stack assumptions before research would turn hypotheses into compatibility commitments.

## Scope

Applies to all five ROADMAP-0001 research steps and every promoted v0.0.1-v0.0.5 iteration.

## Enforcement

Changed-file scope review must confirm that Wave 1 changes are limited to governed research/documentation/recovery surfaces. The roadmap itself and AUDIT-0001 make the absence of production runtime code an acceptance gate.

## Exception process

A need for empirical runtime execution requires a separately authorized non-research roadmap/step or an explicit ROADMAP revision. It may not be smuggled into a research-only step.

## Consequences

Violating this boundary would create implementation authority before capture/security and persistent/public contracts have been synthesized.

## Evidence

`REFERENCE-0001`, `ROADMAP-0001`, and `agents/governance/research-only-steps.md`.

