# CONSTRAINT-0003 - Explicit Watch, Local-First, and Payload-Minimized Observation

## Constraint

The baseline crsniffer product MUST collect network-resource observations only while the user has explicitly activated **Watch** for a selected tab. Observation data MUST remain local by default and MUST exclude request/response bodies, form/post payloads, credential-bearing headers, cookies, and WebSocket/EventSource message payloads from the baseline capture contract.

Service-worker restart may reconcile an already-active Watch intent when its target and authority still exist, but browser/profile restart MUST NOT silently restart observation. Stop, tab close, or permission loss MUST terminate new observation immediately.

## Rationale / source

Chrome treats browsing activity as sensitive user data and permits it when necessary for a prominently described user-facing feature. Chrome's network APIs can expose materially more data than crsniffer needs. A user-visible Watch boundary and payload minimization align the product's single purpose with the least data necessary to provide it.

## Scope

All future capture adapters, session state, resource observation models, persistence, diagnostics, exports, page-field enrichment, and UI flows.

## Enforcement

- ROADMAP-0001 STEP-02/03/04/05 must preserve this floor or explicitly revise/supersede this constraint.
- Future implementation tests must prove no observation outside active Watch and no baseline payload/credential capture.
- Security/privacy review must inspect diagnostics/export/telemetry surfaces for raw browsing-data leakage.

## Exception process

Any need to capture bodies, credential-bearing headers, message payloads, or silently resume across browser restart requires a new or revised ADR plus explicit security/privacy evidence and user-facing disclosure. It cannot be introduced as an implementation convenience.

## Consequences

Violating this constraint would expand the Chrome permission/data-risk surface beyond the user-requested resource-sniffing purpose, weaken store-policy defensibility, and make background behavior surprising.

## Evidence

REFERENCE-0004 revision 2, FINDING-0009, FINDING-0010, MATRIX-0004, STEP-01 research-data capture.

## Revision history

