# CONSTRAINT-0004 - Immutable Observation and Frozen Declarative Watch Rule Contract

## Constraint

Baseline crsniffer MUST preserve captured network facts as immutable observation history. Duplicate folding, classification presentation, filtering and Packagizer actions MUST be explicit derived/evaluation layers and MUST NOT destructively rewrite the raw observation identity/history.

Starting Watch MUST freeze the effective type/glob/rule/template definitions for that WatchSession. Rules/templates MUST be declarative and deterministic; they MUST NOT execute arbitrary JavaScript/eval, expose baseline credential/cookie/body/raw-payload tokens, or depend on hidden mutation of source facts from earlier rule actions.

Packagizer changes MUST apply to newly admitted resources under the frozen session contract and MUST NOT silently retroactively mutate existing observation history.

## Rationale / source

Chrome request identity differs from URL identity; JDownloader provides useful ordered/new-item/stop/Test behavior but permits hidden rule-data coupling and empty-string missing properties; Cat Catch demonstrates token/transformation ergonomics while exposing a broader sensitive-data vocabulary than crsniffer's baseline allows. CONSTRAINT-0003 already requires local-first payload minimization.

## Scope

Future observation schema, dedup projection, classification, filter admission, saved definitions, WatchSession snapshots, rule evaluator, template/token engine, preview/explanation, persistence, exports and UI.

## Enforcement

- STEP-03/04/05 must preserve or explicitly supersede this constraint.
- Future implementation tests must prove raw observation immutability, frozen-session definitions, source-versus-derived separation, missing-value handling, safe token allowlist and preview/live evaluator parity.
- Security/privacy review must reject credentials/bodies/raw payloads or arbitrary executable transforms entering baseline tokens/evaluation.

## Exception process

Weakening immutability, adding arbitrary code execution, exposing sensitive token families, or enabling silent retroactive re-evaluation requires explicit new/revised ADR plus security/privacy evidence and user-visible semantics; it cannot be introduced as implementation convenience.

## Consequences

Violation makes history non-reproducible, preview explanations unreliable, session behavior dependent on editing timing, and browsing-data exposure materially broader than the declared product purpose.

## Evidence

REFERENCE-0002 revision 3, REFERENCE-0003 revision 2, REFERENCE-0007, FINDING-0011 through FINDING-0016, MATRIX-0005 through MATRIX-0007, STEP-02 research-data capture.

