# CONSTRAINT-0005 - Exact-Document Page Enrichment and Frozen Referenced Mapping Contract

## Constraint

Baseline crsniffer page enrichment MUST be bound to an exact watched top-level document context. `tabId`, frame ID, current tab URL, timing proximity, or a later replacement document MUST NOT be used as a substitute for missing/ambiguous `topDocumentId` attribution.

A new committed top-level `documentId` MUST invalidate previous page-field snapshots for future enrichment. Same-document History API/fragment transitions MUST invalidate reusable snapshot results through a page-revision generation even though the document ID remains stable. Arbitrary DOM mutation MUST NOT be represented as fully tracked unless a later explicit architecture adds and justifies such tracking.

Referenced page fields MUST evaluate on demand against the exact target document and produce immutable PageFieldSnapshots whose context/result identity is checked before consumption. Stale, unavailable, inactive, permission-inaccessible, or unattributed context MUST fail closed to Missing/unavailable rather than re-evaluating against whatever page is currently visible.

Starting Watch MUST freeze the exact PageFieldMapping definitions referenced by the effective enabled rules/templates, extending CONSTRAINT-0004's frozen-definition contract. Unreferenced mapping definitions MAY remain independently mutable.

Page mappings MUST remain declarative/deterministic. Baseline MUST reject arbitrary JavaScript/eval, dotted arbitrary property traversal, DOM/function objects as property results, and automatic raw `innerHTML`/`outerHTML` capture. Page/field source facts MUST remain immutable during Packagizer evaluation.

## Rationale / source

Chrome document IDs are unique per document while frame IDs can persist across navigation; same-document history/fragment events update URL without changing document ID; webRequest and webNavigation have no defined cross-API ordering. Chrome scripting can target exact document IDs and returns document identity for result validation. DOM/XPath standards preserve typed results and mutation-sensitive iterator/snapshot distinctions. STEP-02 already requires immutable source facts and frozen Watch definitions.

## Scope

Future PageContext/ResourceObservation attribution, page mapping definitions, scripting/content communication, candidate/read/cardinality/transform logic, field dependency resolution, Packagizer token context, Preview, persistence and diagnostics.

## Enforcement

- STEP-04/05 must preserve or explicitly supersede this constraint.
- Future implementation tests must prove stale-document rejection, same-document invalidation, exact-document result verification, fail-closed unattributed resources, frozen referenced mapping definitions, Missing/falsey distinctions and Preview/live parity.
- Any caching/MutationObserver optimization must prove semantic equivalence to on-demand exact-document evaluation.

## Exception process

Weakening exact-document attribution, enabling ambient continuous page scraping, exposing markup/raw DOM broadly, or adding executable user mapping code requires explicit ADR/security/privacy evidence and cannot be introduced as an implementation convenience.

## Consequences

Violation can attach the wrong title/episode/series/page metadata to a resource after navigation, create non-reproducible rules, or broaden browsing-content collection beyond the product's declared purpose.

## Evidence

REFERENCE-0004 revision 4, REFERENCE-0008, REFERENCE-0009, FINDING-0017 through FINDING-0022, MATRIX-0008 through MATRIX-0010, STEP-03 research-data.

