# FINDING-0001 - Network Observation Permission Shape Is a Primary Architecture Risk

## Source fact

Chrome documents webRequest observation as permission- and host-authority-sensitive. `activeTab` temporarily supplies main-frame-origin authority, while `chrome.debugger` can instrument Network but requires the explicit debugger permission. MV3 service-worker state is interruption-prone.

## Source / evidence

REFERENCE-0004 and the 20260819 research-data capture.

## Interpretation

A resource sniffer that aims to see third-party CDN/media requests cannot assume the exact-origin scripting permission model of a page scraper. Capture completeness, user warning surface, runtime lifecycle, and trust boundary are coupled.

## Repository implication

STEP-01 must compare webRequest, debugger/CDP Network, browser/page timing/DOM supplementation, and a layered design. v0.0.0 intentionally selects none.

## Confidence / limitations

High confidence in the documented permission/lifecycle facts; actual coverage behavior across cache, service workers, redirects, WebSocket/media, and third-party origins remains STEP-01 research.

## Follow-up

