# FINDING-0010 - Baseline Resource Observation Must Minimize Sensitive Payloads

## Source fact

Chrome network/debugger APIs can expose URLs, headers, request bodies, response bodies, cookies, WebSocket frames, and other browsing data depending on API/options. Chrome Web Store Limited Use permits browsing-activity handling only as necessary for a prominently described user-facing feature, and Chrome messaging guidance treats content-script input as untrusted.

## Source / evidence

REFERENCE-0004 revision 2 and the STEP-01 research-data capture.

## Interpretation

API availability is not product necessity. Crsniffer's stated baseline purpose is finding and organizing resource URLs, not capturing page credentials or payload content.

## Repository implication

The baseline candidate observation envelope may include URL/method/type/time/status/MIME/size/cache/redirect/error and tab/frame/document attribution, with narrowly allowlisted metadata needed for classification/naming. Bodies, form data, Cookie/Set-Cookie/Authorization-class headers, WebSocket message payloads, and remote browsing-data telemetry are excluded.

## Confidence / limitations

High. STEP-02 will refine the exact resource observation schema and safe response-metadata allowlist.

