# FINDING-0011 - WebRequest Request Identity Is a Logical Trace Not a URL or Physical HTTP Hop

## Source fact

Chrome states that `requestId` remains constant over one web-request lifecycle and that redirect/authentication can map several physical HTTP requests to one web request.

## Source / evidence

REFERENCE-0007 and Chrome `webRequest` Request IDs/lifecycle documentation refreshed 2026-08-19.

## Interpretation

A URL is neither a safe raw-observation primary key nor proof of one physical network transfer. Redirect hops belong to one logical trace; a later same-URL request with a different request ID is a separate observation.

## Repository implication

Model immutable `ResourceObservation` identity as `(WatchSession, requestId)` and put URL-based duplicate folding in a separate projection. Preserve ordered redirect facts rather than rewriting history.

## Confidence / limitations

High for Chrome request identity. Cross-browser portability is not yet evaluated.

