# FINDING-0012 - Resource Classification Must Preserve Evidence and Must Not Equate Chrome Media With Video

## Source fact

Chrome defines `ResourceType` by request usage and provides a generic `media` value. WHATWG groups MIME types independently, and IANA registers HLS/DASH manifest media types under `application/*`.

## Source / evidence

REFERENCE-0007; Chrome ResourceType, WHATWG MIME Sniffing and IANA media-type registry.

## Interpretation

No single signal gives a complete "video" truth. Treating Chrome `media` as video would admit audio and ambiguous resources; treating extension as authoritative would misclassify signed or misleading URLs.

## Repository implication

Preserve MIME essence, Chrome type, URL extension and classification reason separately. Default Images means semantic `image`; default Videos means semantic `video` plus `stream_manifest`, not generic `media` or audio. Unknown remains possible because body sniffing is excluded.

## Confidence / limitations

High for semantic separation; the exact bounded extension table is a future implementation detail subject to STEP-05 acceptance.

## Follow-up

