# FINDING-0013 - Custom Resource Globs Need a Minimal Grammar Distinct From Chrome Permission Match Patterns

## Source fact

Chrome documents simple `*`/`?` globs for content-script inclusion/exclusion and separately documents structured scheme/host/path match patterns used by extension permission/matching surfaces.

## Source / evidence

REFERENCE-0007 and current Chrome content-script/match-pattern documentation.

## Interpretation

Using the term or parser "match pattern" for crsniffer resource filtering would couple product filtering to Chrome permission syntax. A bounded glob can be easier to explain, validate and reuse in Packagizer conditions.

## Repository implication

Adopt a dedicated whole-canonical-URL resource-glob v1: `*`, `?`, backslash escaping, case-sensitive full-string matching, include OR, exclude veto; reject regex/extglob/brace/classes in baseline.

## Confidence / limitations

High for syntax distinction. Exact implementation/parser tests belong to Wave 2.

## Follow-up

MATRIX-0006, ROADMAP-0001 STEP-05.

