# FINDING-0014 - Packagizer Ordering Should Transform a Derived Projection Without Hidden Source Mutation

## Source fact

JDownloader rules are ordered, can stop later processing, apply to newly added items, and higher rules can mutate filename/package data such that later rules match differently.

## Source / evidence

REFERENCE-0003 revision 2 and official Packagizer documentation refreshed 2026-08-19.

## Interpretation

Ordering/stop semantics are useful, but allowing earlier derived assignments to silently mutate the source facts read by later conditions makes previews and reproducibility harder.

## Repository implication

Rules should evaluate top-to-bottom against one immutable source token context. Actions write a separate derived projection; later action assignments may intentionally overwrite earlier derived fields, but later conditions do not see those mutations. Successful `stop_processing` remains available.

## Confidence / limitations

Medium-high: this is an evidence-backed crsniffer adaptation, not an upstream requirement; final normativity belongs to STEP-05.

## Follow-up

MATRIX-0007, CONSTRAINT-0004, ROADMAP-0001 STEP-05.

