# FINDING-0021 - Reusable Page Mappings Should Freeze Only Referenced Watch Dependencies

## Source fact

The product intent requires reusable named page fields, while STEP-02 already freezes effective rule/template definitions at Watch start. The crscraper donor models mapping fields as reusable definitions with ordered extraction candidates rather than mandatory per-run inline selectors.

## Source / evidence

CONSTRAINT-0004, MATRIX-0007, REFERENCE-0008 donor inspection, ROADMAP-0001 STEP-03 product requirement.

## Interpretation

Forcing all page mappings into every WatchSession would bloat the common Watch path and freeze unrelated configuration. Leaving referenced mappings mutable would make session results depend on edit timing and break Preview/replay explanations.

## Repository implication

Maintain a reusable `PageFieldMapping` library separate from the primary Watch flow. Resolve field dependencies from enabled frozen rules/templates when Watch starts and freeze only those referenced mapping definitions into the WatchSession effective configuration. Unreferenced mappings remain independently editable. A mapping field owns ordered complete candidates, not one global selector plus fragmented fallback settings.

## Confidence / limitations

High for dependency/freeze semantics. Storage representation and editor layout belong to STEP-04/implementation planning.

## Follow-up

MATRIX-0010, CONSTRAINT-0005, ROADMAP-0001 STEP-04/05.

