# FINDING-0023 - WXT Vue and TypeScript Are the Strongest crsniffer Stack Candidate Without Freezing Stale Pins

## Source fact

WXT provides extension-specific entrypoints and manifest generation, recognizes background/content/Side Panel surfaces, and has first-party Vue + TypeScript starter support. Plasmo provides comparable extension abstractions but is React-first with optional Vue support. Vite is a generic web build tool and does not itself own extension manifest/entrypoint semantics. Current WXT documentation renders v0.21.4 while the v0.0.38 donor still pins WXT 0.21.3.

## Source / evidence

REFERENCE-0010, REFERENCE-0011, refreshed official WXT/Plasmo/Vite/Vue documentation.

## Interpretation

WXT + Vue 3 + TypeScript + MV3 + Side Panel minimizes bespoke extension wiring while staying aligned with the donor team's current design language. The one-patch WXT mismatch is evidence that exact package pins should not be copied from a donor or frozen during research.

## Repository implication

Adopt the stack family as the preferred STEP-04 denominator for STEP-05 synthesis. Do not add `wxt.config.*`, Vue source, runtime dependencies or a lockfile in Wave 1. The first ROADMAP-0002 scaffold step must fresh-check current exact versions and create a reproducible lockfile. Prefer Vue Composition API / `<script setup lang="ts">`; do not require Vue Router, Pinia, Bootstrap/Tailwind or a component kit until concrete UI complexity justifies them.

## Confidence / limitations

High for stack-family fit; exact versions/toolchain and optional state/styling libraries remain implementation-time facts.

## Follow-up

MATRIX-0011, CONSTRAINT-0006, ROADMAP-0001 STEP-05.

