# FINDING-0024 - The Side Panel Should Be the Primary Command and Presentation Plane but Never Durable Authority

## Source fact

Chrome Side Panel is a persistent companion extension surface alongside the current page. Extension Side Panel pages can use extension APIs, while MV3 background workers can terminate independently. The crscraper donor also treats its Side Panel as hydrated presentation rather than canonical persistence.

## Source / evidence

REFERENCE-0010, REFERENCE-0012, Chrome Side Panel and service-worker documentation.

## Interpretation

The product's Watch-first workflow fits a persistent Side Panel better than a transient popup or DevTools-only UI, but durable Watch/session/history truth cannot live in Vue component state.

## Repository implication

Prefer a Side Panel as primary UI. The background/service-worker domain owns privileged commands, capture/evaluation coordination and persistence writes; IndexedDB owns durable truth. The Side Panel is a query/command/projection client that must rehydrate after panel close/reopen or worker restart. Popup and DevTools surfaces are rejected from the baseline; a separate Options page is deferred unless Side Panel settings prove too cramped.

## Confidence / limitations

High for primary-surface disposition. Exact component boundaries and message schemas belong to later implementation.

## Follow-up

MATRIX-0011, MATRIX-0013, CONSTRAINT-0006.

