# FINDING-0026 - Active Watch Correctness Must Not Depend on Service Worker or Port Liveness

## Source fact

MV3 service workers are event-driven and may be terminated after inactivity. `storage.session` survives worker shutdown. Long-lived message channels can support communication but are not durable state.

## Source / evidence

REFERENCE-0012, CONSTRAINT-0003, current Chrome service-worker lifecycle documentation.

## Interpretation

Keeping a Port open or an in-memory background singleton alive would make capture correctness depend on a browser lifecycle behavior the platform explicitly does not guarantee.

## Repository implication

The runtime topology must reconstruct active Watch intent from persisted/session authority whenever the worker wakes, while browser/profile restart remains a deliberate non-resume boundary. Side Panel streaming may use a reconnecting Port for low-latency deltas, but the panel must also support bounded query/rehydration from canonical persistence. Capture/evaluation state transitions need idempotent commands and observable degraded/error states.

## Confidence / limitations

High architectural requirement; exact event/listener registration and recovery sequence belongs to implementation.

## Follow-up

MATRIX-0012, MATRIX-0013, CONSTRAINT-0006.

