# FINDING-0027 - Watch-First Progressive Disclosure Should Keep Rules Fields Permissions and Diagnostics Contextual

## Source fact

Chrome recommends Side Panels that complement browsing with little distraction, and extension/store guidance favors simple understandable single-purpose UI. The accepted product intent makes Watch the primary CTA and treats rules/mappings/diagnostics as supporting surfaces.

## Source / evidence

REFERENCE-0012, docs/product-intent.md, CONSTRAINT-0003 through CONSTRAINT-0005.

## Interpretation

A tab-heavy control console would invert the product hierarchy. Most users should be able to start/stop Watch, see resource results and change Images/Videos filters without entering Packagizer or mapping editors.

## Repository implication

Prefer three top-level Side Panel destinations: **Watch**, **Rules**, **Settings**. Watch is default and contains current tab/context, primary Watch/Stop, readiness/permission state, compact Images/Videos filters, advanced include/exclude globs, a virtualized live resource stream and selected-resource detail. Rules contains ordered Packagizer rules/templates with contextual Token Browser, Preview/Test and referenced Page Fields. Settings contains retention/Clear, privacy/support/diagnostics and local preferences. Permission grant/retry/revoke and diagnostics are contextual states, not primary navigation destinations.

## Confidence / limitations

High for hierarchy; exact visual layout/components remain implementation and usability-test work.

## Follow-up

MATRIX-0013, CONSTRAINT-0006, ROADMAP-0001 STEP-05.

