# FINDING-0028 - Large Live Resource Streams Need Virtualization Batching and Shallow Presentation State

## Source fact

Vue's official performance guidance recommends virtualizing large lists and using shallow reactive APIs when deep reactivity over large immutable structures creates overhead.

## Source / evidence

REFERENCE-0011 and Vue performance documentation.

## Interpretation

A long Watch can accumulate many resource observations; rendering or deeply-reactivating the complete durable history in a narrow persistent panel will waste memory and degrade interaction.

## Repository implication

The Side Panel should query/hydrate bounded pages, apply append-only incremental updates, keep a bounded in-memory visible window and virtualize/window large result lists. Treat immutable observation rows with shallow presentation reactivity. Batch/throttle summary updates and never require full-history snapshots over messaging. Durable history remains in IndexedDB. v0.0.21 implements this with existing indexed cursors, one-shot bounded queries, a shallow 500-row Side Panel buffer and a pure fixed-row virtual-window calculation; a 10,000-row model test mounts only visible+overscan rows. The current 40-row default page, 100-row maximum page, 500-row raw scan and 500-row UI buffer are controller constants, not product maxima. v0.0.30 STEP-12 measures 10,000-row history/merge workloads and a 100,000-row virtual-window traversal without evidence requiring those constants to change. STEP-12 additionally coalesces burst Port invalidations into a 50ms presentation refresh wave while preserving one-shot query authority.

## Confidence / limitations

High for architecture/performance strategy; exact batch/window sizes and dependency choice are measurement-dependent.

## Follow-up

MATRIX-0013, CONSTRAINT-0006, ROADMAP-0003 STEP-12 measured performance/capacity hardening and STEP-14 final usability certification.

