# FINDING-0031 - Versioned Contracts and Migration Must Start Before User State Exists

## Source fact

The accepted design includes mutable reusable definitions, immutable WatchSession snapshots, durable observations/history, PageFieldSnapshots, derived projections, and cross-context messages. STEP-04 explicitly requires versioned storage topology and migration from the first durable implementation.

## Interpretation

Adding schema/revision/version authority only after users accumulate state would force silent reinterpretation or an avoidable breaking migration. The first implementation must distinguish physical database version from logical object/message schema versions.

## Repository implication

ROADMAP-0002 must establish stable IDs, definition revisions, object/message `schemaVersion`/`protocolVersion`, immutable frozen-session digests, and migration authority before feature-rich UI depends on persisted state. Physical IndexedDB store topology remains a STEP-03 implementation decision rather than a Wave-1 guess.

## Confidence / limitations

High. Exact schema fields/indexes and migration mechanics require fresh implementation research and executable tests.
</file>

