# FINDING-0033 — Form-first working copies can preserve saved-revision WatchSession authority

## Finding

Crsniffer does not need a new durable draft model to achieve form-first editing. The existing domain already provides the correct publication boundary: mutable revisioned saved definitions are explicitly persisted, then WatchSession composition freezes exact saved revisions and digests into immutable runtime/history authority.

A Side Panel working copy can therefore remain disposable presentation state. Loading a saved definition deep-copies values and source ID/revision provenance into the editor. New or modified values become durable only through explicit `Save as` or revision-checked `Update`. Watch never executes an unsaved working copy; the user must persist Watch-affecting edits before Start uses them.

## Evidence

- `src/definitions/catalog.ts` provides explicit create/update with expected-revision conflict protection.
- `src/definitions/composition.ts` requires a persisted Watch definition and freezes referenced saved revisions/digests.
- `src/watch/controller.ts` resolves a persisted Watch definition before composition and supports the built-in Default Watch path.
- ADR-0004 and ADR-0005 prohibit presentation state from becoming durable/correctness authority.
- Promoted Crscraper v0.0.45 demonstrates the UX value of form-first working copies and explicit preset mutation, but its direct-runnable-draft semantics are not copied because crsniffer has a different accepted execution boundary.

## Consequence

ROADMAP-0003 can deliver structured form-first editors without adding a new IndexedDB store, local/session draft authority, new WatchSession schema or silent autosave. ADR-0006 owns the normative working-copy lifecycle.

## Review / disposition

Accepted for ROADMAP-0003 STEP-01. Reopen only if a later step demonstrates a product requirement for durable unsaved drafts or direct transient Watch execution; that would require explicit architecture and migration review.

