# MATRIX-0005 - Resource Observation Classification and Deduplication Contract

## Question / objective

What observation identity, resource classification and duplicate-folding semantics can remain deterministic without rewriting raw network history or sniffing sensitive payload bodies?

| Concern | Candidate contract | Why | Disposition |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Raw observation identity | `(watch_session_id, request_id)` | Chrome request ID is lifecycle identity | **adopt** |
| Redirect/auth | ordered lifecycle/hop facts on same observation | several HTTP requests can map to one web request | **adopt** |
| Same URL requested again | new observation when request ID differs | URL is not request identity | **retain distinct** |
| User-facing dedup | derived grouping by Watch + document epoch/unknown + canonical final URL without fragment | avoids destructive history rewrite | **adopt projection** |
| Query handling | retain serialized query bytes/order; do not sort/remove | signed/cache-busting URLs can be query-sensitive | **retain** |
| Cross-document dedup | disabled by default | page/document context matters for later fields | **defer/avoid baseline** |
| Primary MIME evidence | parsed response MIME essence | stronger than URL extension | **adopt** |
| HLS/DASH | `stream_manifest` from registered MIME or bounded extension fallback | manifests are video workflow resources but not `video/*` | **adopt** |
| Chrome `image` | useful corroborating/fallback evidence | request usage aligns well with image intent | **adopt** |
| Chrome `media` | never equals video by itself | can include audio/ambiguous media | **reject equivalence** |
| Extension | bounded fallback only if MIME missing/generic/unrecognized | URL names are weak evidence | **adapt** |
| Contradiction | explicit recognized MIME wins over extension; preserve conflict reason | deterministic and explainable | **adopt** |
| Body sniffing | absent | conflicts with baseline payload-minimization scope | **reject baseline** |

## Candidate semantic kinds

`image`, `video`, `stream_manifest`, `audio`, `other`, `unknown`.

Default **Images** selects `image`. Default **Videos** selects `video` + `stream_manifest`. Generic Chrome `media` without decisive MIME/extension remains unknown/ambiguous rather than being promoted to video.

## Interpretation

Raw observations and user-visible resources are not the same identity layer. The observation layer remains lossless within the API evidence available; deduplication is reversible projection with occurrence metadata. Classification is evidence/reason based and admits an explicit `unknown` state.

## Recommendation

Carry this contract candidate into STEP-05; let STEP-04 decide persistence representation/retention, not semantic identity.

## Uncertainty / unresolved questions

Exact fallback extension tables and normalization implementation belong to Wave 2; page/document epoch semantics are refined by STEP-03.

## Review / disposition

Accepted as STEP-02 research authority; not yet an implementation ADR.

## Revision history

| Date | Revision | Change | Status |
| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
| 2026-08-19 | 1 | Establish resource identity/classification/dedup dispositions | active |
