# MATRIX-0006 - Resource Type Preset and Glob Admission Contract

## Question / objective

How should default Images/Videos and custom include/exclude globs combine as a deterministic privacy-preserving resource admission filter?

## Admission formula

`positive = matches_any_selected_type_preset OR matches_any_include_glob`

`admit = positive AND NOT matches_any_exclude_glob`

If no type preset is selected and include-glob list is empty, `positive=false`: admit nothing.

| Scenario | Result | Rationale |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Default configuration | Images + Videos positive lanes | requested product floor |
| Semantic image | admit by Images unless excluded | direct default |
| Semantic video | admit by Videos unless excluded | direct default |
| Stream manifest | admit by Videos unless excluded | HLS/DASH are video workflow resources |
| Audio only | not admitted by Videos | avoid generic-media false positives |
| Unknown resource + matching include glob | admit | glob is explicit user positive lane |
| Type miss + include-glob hit | admit | type/glob positives are OR |
| Type hit + exclude-glob hit | reject | exclude is final veto |
| Include hit + exclude hit | reject | exclude wins |
| No positive lane | reject all | fail-safe and privacy-preserving |

## Resource-glob v1 grammar

- target: full canonical URL serialization without fragment;
- `*`: zero or more characters;
- `?`: exactly one character;
- `\\*`, `\\?`, `\\\\`: literal escapes; trailing `\\` invalid;
- matching is case-sensitive; canonical URL parsing normalizes scheme/host as the platform defines while path/query remain significant;
- full-string matching; users add `*` for contains behavior;
- multiple includes OR; multiple excludes OR; exclude vetoes;
- no `**`, braces, character classes, extglobs, captures or regex mode in v1;
- invalid patterns fail definition validation before Watch starts.

## Admission versus UI hiding

The baseline filter is an admission/persistence boundary, not merely a list-display filter. The observer may inspect minimum transient facts needed to classify/match, but non-admitted resources are not retained as normal history. A later UI may add purely visual filtering over already-admitted data without changing this admission contract.

## Recommendation

Adopt the formula/grammar as STEP-02 contract candidate. Reuse the same glob operator for Packagizer string conditions so there is one wildcard mental model.

## Uncertainty / unresolved questions

STEP-04 owns editor UX/persistence. STEP-05 decides final contract/versioning.

## Review / disposition

Accepted as STEP-02 research authority; no parser/runtime is implemented here.

