# MATRIX-0007 - Packagizer Rule Token Template and Preview Contract

## Question / objective

Which Packagizer behaviors should crsniffer retain/adapt/reject so resource naming/grouping remains declarative, deterministic, previewable and privacy-safe?

| Behavior | JDownloader/Cat Catch evidence | crsniffer disposition |
| --- | --- | --- |
| ordered rules | Packagizer has explicit rule order | **adopt** |
| stop further rules | Packagizer supports stop checkbox | **adopt** after successful matched rule |
| newly-added semantics | Packagizer does not retroactively mutate existing links | **adopt** for newly admitted observations |
| rule Test/preview | both products expose testing/preview concepts | **adopt**, same evaluator as live |
| earlier actions alter later conditions | JDownloader can behave this way | **reject hidden mutation** |
| exact `<jd:...>` syntax | JDownloader-specific | **reject** |
| `${...}` token ergonomics | Cat Catch precedent | **adapt** to namespaced crsniffer tokens |
| missing property -> empty | current JDownloader behavior | **reject**; preserve Missing sentinel |
| environment/plugin-property tokens | JDownloader-specific/powerful | **reject baseline** |
| cookie/raw-data/user-agent tokens | Cat Catch supports some | **reject baseline** under CONSTRAINT-0003 |
| arbitrary JS/eval | unnecessary for product floor | **reject baseline** |
| regex transforms/conditions | upstream precedent but complexity/perf risk | **defer** |
| safe transforms | Cat Catch shows chained transforms | **adapt** bounded whitelist |
| import/export | Packagizer has it | **defer** UX/file format to later roadmap |

## Rule evaluation contract candidate

1. Watch start freezes an immutable effective rule/filter/template snapshot.
2. Enabled rules run top-to-bottom.
3. Conditions within a rule are ANDed and read only immutable source context.
4. Matched rule actions write a derived projection only.
5. Later rule actions may intentionally overwrite prior derived fields, but later conditions do not read those mutations.
6. If any action template in a matched rule fails, apply none of that rule's actions, emit bounded error explanation, and stop later rules for that candidate.
7. `stop_processing=true` stops later rules only after the matched rule applies successfully.
8. Rule edits affect future WatchSessions/new observations, not existing history.

## Condition vocabulary candidate

`exists`, `missing`, `equals`, `not_equals`, `contains`, `starts_with`, `ends_with`, `glob`, plus typed numeric `< <= > >=` for numeric facts. Case behavior must be explicit per condition or fixed by operator; no implicit locale-dependent comparison.

## Token/template candidate

Source namespace in STEP-02: `${resource.url}`, `${resource.host}`, `${resource.path}`, `${resource.filename}`, `${resource.basename}`, `${resource.extension}`, `${resource.mime}`, `${resource.kind}`, `${resource.chrome_type}`, `${resource.status}`, `${resource.content_length}`, `${resource.initiator}`, `${resource.observed_at}`, `${watch.started_at}`.

STEP-03-populated exact-context sources: `${page.url}`, `${page.title}`, `${page.origin}`, `${field.<slug>}` under MATRIX-0009/MATRIX-0010 and CONSTRAINT-0005. These remain immutable source facts and fail to Missing on stale/unattributed page context.

Missing is not empty. Unknown token/transform/syntax invalidates the definition before Watch. Safe transform candidate set: `default`, `trim`, `lower`, `upper`, `slice`, literal `replace`, `urlencode`, `filename_safe`. No cookie/credential/body/raw-header/environment/plugin-property tokens.

## Preview/explanation candidate

The preview uses the same pure evaluator and reports classification reason; positive/exclude filter decisions; rule order; condition result; token state; transform result; action before/after; stop/error reason. Durable diagnostics retain structural IDs/outcomes/error codes, not raw URL/token values by default.

## Recommendation

Carry the declarative/frozen/derived-projection model into STEP-05. STEP-03 has now populated page-aware token sources through exact-document PageFieldSnapshots without weakening source/derived separation.

## Uncertainty / unresolved questions

Exact public serialization, import/export, UI editor, platform filename/path sanitization and explicit historical re-evaluation are later concerns.

## Review / disposition

Accepted as STEP-02 research authority; not production code or final ADR.

## Revision history

| Date | Revision | Change | Status |
