# MATRIX-0008 - Page Selector Read Cardinality Fallback and Transform Contract

## Question / objective

Define the smallest deterministic page-field extraction envelope that preserves real CSS/XPath result semantics, Missing/falsey distinctions, candidate fallback, and privacy-safe reads.

| Concern | Evidence | STEP-03 disposition |
| --- | --- | --- |
| CSS result shape | DOM `querySelectorAll()` is static and node-oriented | **adopt** ordered static node array |
| XPath node result | XPath supports iterator/snapshot; iterator invalidates on mutation | **adopt** ordered node snapshot normalization |
| XPath scalar result | XPath can return string/number/boolean | **adopt** typed scalar; do not coerce to node/string early |
| missing attribute | DOM returns null for absent attribute | **adopt** Missing distinct from empty attribute |
| `textContent` | structural descendant text | **adopt** `text_content` read |
| `innerText` | rendered text semantics | **adopt** `inner_text` read |
| attribute | common deterministic page metadata | **adopt** `attribute(name)` |
| property | useful for href/src/value-like IDL state | **adapt** direct single property name, primitive result only; no dotted traversal/functions/DOM objects |
| XPath scalar | already a typed value | **adopt** `raw` only for XPath scalar results |
| inner/outer HTML | serializes markup, expands data/sensitivity/size | **defer baseline** |
| cardinality | donor precedent + explicit ambiguity control | **adopt** `first`, `optional_one`, `exact_one`, `many` |
| candidate fallback | failures have different meanings | **adopt** next candidate only on Missing or explicit rejection; evaluation/read/cardinality/transform/validation errors stop |
| transforms | STEP-02 already requires safe declarative transforms | **adapt** one shared typed registry; page subset `trim`, `lower`, `upper`, `slice`, literal `replace`, `to_string`, `join` |
| arbitrary JS/eval | high security/reproducibility cost | **reject baseline** |

## Candidate field definition

A reusable field owns an ordered list of complete candidates. Each candidate contains selector family/query, optional XPath namespace bindings, read operation, cardinality, deterministic transforms, and explicit acceptance policy. Field-level default/required/validation runs after candidate resolution.

Candidate selector families:

- CSS: static ordered node result.
- XPath: typed string/number/boolean or ordered node snapshot result.

Candidate read modes:

- nodes: `text_content`, `inner_text`, `attribute(name)`, `property(name)`;
- XPath scalar: `raw`;
- no baseline markup serialization read.

Cardinality:

- `first`: Missing if zero, first value if one or more;
- `optional_one`: Missing if zero, value if one, error if more than one;
- `exact_one`: error unless exactly one;
- `many`: ordered list; direct string template use requires an explicit scalarizing transform such as `join`.

Missing/null/empty string/false/zero remain distinct. A default applies only to Missing. `required` requires presence; it does not silently mean nonblank. Blank rejection is explicit candidate acceptance/validation.

## Error/fallback contract

Fallback is semantic, not exception swallowing. Missing or an explicit acceptance rejection may try the next candidate. Invalid selector syntax, XPath evaluation error, disallowed property shape, cardinality violation, transform type error, or validation error produces an explicit field error and does not silently fall through.

## Recommendation

Carry this typed/snapshot/missing-aware extraction envelope into STEP-05. Keep markup reads and arbitrary executable transforms outside the baseline unless later evidence explicitly reopens them.

## Review / disposition

Accepted as STEP-03 research authority; not production code or final ADR.

