# MATRIX-0009 - Page Context Navigation SPA Staleness and Attribution Contract

## Question / objective

When may page-derived values be considered valid for a captured resource across top-level navigation, SPA/history changes, child frames, lifecycle transitions and races between network/navigation events?

| Scenario | Platform fact/risk | STEP-03 contract |
| --- | --- | --- |
| new top-level commit | frameId can stay 0 while documentId changes | create new PageContext; prior snapshots stale immediately |
| History API `pushState`/`replaceState` | same documentId, updated URL event | retain document identity, increment `pageRevision`, invalidate reusable snapshot |
| fragment navigation | same documentId, updated URL event | same as History API revision invalidation |
| arbitrary DOM mutation | no universal navigation event | no freshness claim from event cache; evaluate referenced fields on demand |
| BFCache restore | DOMContentLoaded may not fire; document lifecycle can change | do not rely on DOMContentLoaded; evaluate when document is active and exact ID is targetable |
| prerender/cached document | same document may be non-active | baseline live page enrichment requires active top-level context; otherwise unavailable until active |
| pending result crosses navigation | old and new documents can coexist/race | compare returned documentId/context revision before consumption; discard stale result |
| webRequest near navigation | no defined ordering with webNavigation | retain attribution status; ambiguous resource-to-page binding yields Missing |
| main-frame resource | request/document evidence can identify top document | bind to captured topDocumentId when exact |
| subframe resource | initiator document differs from visible page | may use top-page fields only with reliable captured frame-to-topDocument attribution; otherwise Missing |
| tab close / permission loss | exact document no longer available | terminate new enrichment; never retarget a new/current tab document |

## PageContext candidate

`PageContext = WatchSessionId + tabId + topDocumentId + pageRevision`.

`topDocumentId` is identity; URL, origin and title are snapshot facts. `pageRevision` is a monotonic invalidation generation for same-document navigation and explicit refresh. It is not presented as a complete DOM mutation counter.

Each ResourceObservation retains initiating-document evidence plus an explicit top-document attribution such as `topDocumentId? + attributionStatus`. Page enrichment requires a valid topDocumentId association with the PageContext used for evaluation.

## Evaluation/freshness candidate

1. Resolve whether the ResourceObservation has a reliable topDocumentId attribution.
2. Resolve/freeze the exact PageContext identity/revision.
3. Execute required page-field dependencies on demand against `documentIds:[topDocumentId]` in an isolated extension-world candidate.
4. Require returned result identity to match the requested document and still-valid page revision before consumption.
5. Emit an immutable PageFieldSnapshot for that rule/template evaluation.
6. If the document is absent, inactive, changed, ambiguous, or permission-inaccessible, return Missing/unavailable with a structural reason; do not evaluate the current replacement document.

## Recommendation

Use documentId as the hard stale boundary and fail closed at attribution/navigation races. Defer performance caching to STEP-04/implementation planning unless it can preserve identical semantics.

## Review / disposition

Accepted as STEP-03 research authority; not production code or final ADR.

## Revision history

| Date | Revision | Change | Status |
| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
| 2026-08-19 | 1 | Define document/page revision, SPA, staleness and attribution dispositions | active |
</file>

