# MATRIX-0010 - Page Field Token Dependency Preview and Reuse Contract

## Question / objective

How should reusable page mappings become safe immutable Packagizer source tokens without making the common Watch path a continuously running page scraper?

| Behavior | STEP-03 disposition |
| --- | --- |
| built-in page facts | adopt `${page.url}`, `${page.origin}`, `${page.title}` from exact PageContext snapshot |
| named mapped facts | adopt `${field.<slug>}` from frozen referenced PageFieldMapping |
| field slug | stable lowercase serialization key: `^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,63}$`; dots reserved for namespace separation |
| source mutability | page/field values are immutable source facts during one evaluator invocation; Packagizer actions cannot mutate them |
| dependency discovery | resolve field tokens used by enabled frozen rules/templates at Watch start |
| freeze scope | freeze only referenced mapping definitions into effective WatchSession configuration; unrelated mappings remain editable |
| evaluation timing | evaluate referenced fields on demand for live rule/template use or explicit Preview |
| missing/stale | preserve Missing plus structural reason; never substitute current replacement document |
| list-valued field | preserve typed list; string template use needs explicit `join`/other scalarizing transform |
| Preview | same mapping + Packagizer semantic evaluators as live; show candidate/read/cardinality/transform/outcome trace |
| persistent diagnostics | retain IDs/stages/outcomes/error codes/context identity; raw page values/markup not persisted by default |
| continuous MutationObserver/page scraping | reject baseline |
| arbitrary JS mapping transform | reject baseline |
| subframe mapping editor | defer; baseline mappings target top-level watched page |
| exact visual editor/navigation | defer to STEP-04 |

## PageFieldSnapshot candidate

A transient/live snapshot contains WatchSession identity; PageContext `tabId`, `topDocumentId`, `pageRevision`, URL/origin/title; mapping ID + revision/content hash for every referenced field; evaluation timestamp; typed field outcome (`resolved`, `missing`, `error`, `unavailable/stale`) and value when locally needed; and structural candidate/evaluation diagnostics.

Persisted history/diagnostics must follow existing local-first/redaction constraints; raw mapped page values are not automatically durable just because they were visible in Preview.

## Reuse/UX boundary

Page Field Mappings are a reusable supporting configuration surface. Watch remains the primary CTA. Rule/template editing may reference field slugs and show dependency readiness; a dedicated mapping Preview may evaluate the current exact page and explain candidate outcomes. Detailed panel layout, keyboard interaction and progressive disclosure belong to STEP-04.

## Recommendation

Populate the reserved `page.*`/`field.*` source namespaces with this exact-document, dependency-frozen model and preserve STEP-02 source/derived separation.

## Review / disposition

Accepted as STEP-03 research authority; not production code or final ADR.

