# MATRIX-0011 - App Stack Build Frontend and Browser Denominator Disposition

## Question / objective

Which application/build/frontend denominator best implements the accepted capture/rule/page contracts with minimal extension-specific glue and without freezing stale tool versions during research?

| Candidate / behavior | Disposition | Reason |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Chrome MV3 | adopt | current Chrome extension platform denominator |
| Side Panel primary surface | adopt | persistent companion UI suits Watch/resource stream; popup is too transient |
| Chrome minimum 116+ | preferred candidate | retains Side Panel base and permits `sidePanel.open()` from user interaction; avoids a 114/115 compatibility branch |
| WXT | adopt stack-family candidate | extension-specific entrypoints/manifest/dev/build/zip and framework flexibility |
| Vue 3 Composition API + TypeScript | adopt | mature typed component model, donor continuity, shallow-reactivity/performance guidance |
| Plasmo + Vue | adapt/reject baseline | capable but React-first; adds less value for Vue-oriented team conventions than WXT |
| plain Vite + hand-authored extension integration | reject baseline | generic web build tool; unnecessary manifest/entrypoint/lifecycle glue |
| exact WXT/Vue/TS/Node/npm pins | defer | refresh during first implementation scaffold and seal with lockfile |
| Vue Router | defer | three small Side Panel destinations can use explicit internal navigation first |
| Pinia/global state library | defer | Side Panel state is projection; add only if measured complexity warrants |
| Bootstrap/Tailwind/component kit | reject baseline requirement | not needed to establish semantic compact Side Panel; styling dependency must earn scope |
| native semantic HTML + CSS variables/scoped CSS | adopt baseline direction | smallest accessibility-first presentation denominator |
| popup primary UI | reject | transient and conflicts with Watch/live-stream primary workflow |
| DevTools panel primary UI | reject | overly specialized/permission-contextual; not the user-facing product purpose |
| separate Options page | defer | Settings fits Side Panel unless implementation evidence proves otherwise |

## Runtime topology candidate

- Background MV3 service worker: privileged Watch lifecycle, capture/classification/evaluation coordination, permission/readiness checks and canonical persistence writes.
- Side Panel: presentation/query/command plane only; reconnects and rehydrates.
- Exact-document field evaluation: on-demand `chrome.scripting` lane under CONSTRAINT-0005; no ambient content-script baseline required by research.
- Versioned command/query/event message contracts; a Port may stream deltas but is not durability authority.

## Recommendation

Carry **MV3 + Chrome 116+ + WXT + Vue 3 + TypeScript + Side Panel** as the preferred STEP-04 denominator into STEP-05. Freeze architecture family, not current package versions.

## Review / disposition

Accepted as STEP-04 research authority; STEP-05 may accept/revise via ADR. No production scaffold is authorized yet.

