# MATRIX-0012 - Persistence Ownership Retention Quota and Recovery Contract

## Question / objective

Which state belongs where so long-running Watch history is durable, browser restart does not silently resume active collection, and Side Panel/service-worker lifetime is never correctness authority?

| State / behavior | STEP-04 disposition |
| --- | --- |
| reusable WatchProfile / PackagizerRule / TemplateDefinition / PageFieldMapping | durable IndexedDB canonical entity with stable identity/revision |
| WatchSession metadata/frozen effective configuration | durable IndexedDB canonical history; active coordination separately session-scoped |
| ResourceObservation | durable IndexedDB canonical raw history after admission; immutable under STEP-02 |
| PageFieldSnapshot | persist only when a live/evaluation/history contract actually requires it; identity/provenance retained, raw field value retention remains minimized |
| derived resource view / dedup projection | recomputable projection unless later performance evidence requires bounded caching |
| redacted diagnostics/history/meta/schema | bounded IndexedDB authority |
| active browser-lifetime Watch coordination | `chrome.storage.session` candidate; survives worker restart, clears browser restart |
| UI route/selection/transient editor state | panel-local/session state, not canonical |
| small local preferences/install metadata | **v0.0.26 implemented:** typed Side Panel defaults in namespaced `chrome.storage.local`; no sync authority |
| observation/rule history in `storage.local` | reject |
| observation/rule history in `storage.sync` | reject |
| `unlimitedStorage` permission baseline | reject; use bounded retention/clear/quota feedback first |
| explicit Clear history / Clear all | **v0.0.26 implemented:** history clears Watch sessions/observations/PageFieldSnapshots/lifecycle while preserving definitions/preferences; all-local additionally clears definitions/preferences and restores only Default Watch; both block while Watch is active and do not revoke Chrome site authority |
| retention | **v0.0.28 implemented:** bounded terminal Watch history; default 30 days / 50 terminal sessions with Settings bounds; active Watch excluded; startup/session-end/policy-change/manual maintenance use the same policy |
| quota monitoring | **v0.0.28 implemented:** `navigator.storage.estimate()` is approximate/advisory; 80% warning / 90% critical presentation signals; pressure may run configured retention early but never widens deletion scope |
| persistence write failure | **v0.0.28 implemented:** normalize storage/quota failure, end active Watch as `storage_failure`, suspend capture, keep terminal pending browser-session trace for retry; never claim a durable observation before IndexedDB commit |
| worker termination | **v0.0.28 implemented:** startup runs logical migration, active-session reconciliation, configured retention and same-browser terminal-pending replay from session authority |
| browser restart | **v0.0.28 re-proven:** session coordination clears with browser restart, so Watch never auto-resumes; durable history/definitions/preferences remain |
| schema version/migration | **v0.0.28 implemented:** physical IndexedDB remains v1/five stores; logical durable authority advances resumably/idempotently v1→v2 with retention/recovery metadata |

## Failure/recovery invariant

A user-visible "Watching" state MUST correspond to an active capture authority capable of persisting admitted observations according to policy. If storage becomes unavailable/quota-exhausted, crsniffer must surface degraded/error status and provide recovery/Clear controls rather than silently continuing with partial history.

## Recommendation

Adopt a three-tier model: **IndexedDB durable domain authority + storage.session browser-lifetime coordination + storage.local small preferences**. Keep storage topology and migration versioned from first implementation.

## Review / disposition

Accepted as STEP-04 research authority; exact physical stores, retention defaults and migration code remain successor implementation work.

## STEP-08 implementation disposition

- Diagnostics expose counts/schema/migration/runtime state only; no URLs, request/document IDs, headers, cookies, bodies, credentials or token values are added.
- Clear operates only on explicit local scopes and is rejected while Watch is active before durable deletion starts.
- Browser-lifetime session/pending-observation coordination is cleared with history; Chrome-granted optional host permissions are a separate authority and are never removed by Clear.
- v0.0.28 / STEP-10 implements automatic bounded retention, advisory quota-pressure handling, logical migration and restart recovery under the narrower disposition below.

## STEP-10 implementation disposition

- Automatic deletion is narrower than explicit Clear: only terminal Watch history outside the configured age/count policy is eligible; definitions/preferences/site permissions are never retention targets.
- Quota pressure is not a second retention policy. Warning/critical estimates only cause the configured policy to run earlier and cannot delete otherwise in-policy canonical history.
- Crsniffer deliberately does not adopt Crscraper's artifact-first pruning because Crsniffer has no equivalent disposable artifact tier.
- Logical migration checkpoints are durable/retryable metadata. A physical IndexedDB version bump/store/index change is not introduced merely to claim migration support.
- `storage_failure` terminates visible Watching state. Terminal pending trace is recovery evidence, not a committed ResourceObservation, and is removed only after durable replay succeeds or explicit Clear/browser-session end removes the session authority.
- Repeated large-history/capacity measurement remains STEP-12; packaged-host permission/security certification remains STEP-11.

## Revision history

| Date | Revision | Change | Status |
| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
| 2026-08-19 | 1 | Define persistence ownership, quota, retention and restart recovery dispositions | active |
| 2026-08-20 | 2 | Record v0.0.26 typed preferences, explicit Clear scopes, structural diagnostics and manual-retention truth while preserving STEP-10 hardening ownership | active |
| 2026-08-20 | 3 | Record v0.0.28 physical-v1/logical-v2 migration, bounded terminal-history retention, advisory quota pressure and storage-failure/restart recovery behavior | active |
</file>

