# MATRIX-0013 - Side Panel Information Architecture Accessibility and Performance Contract

## Question / objective

How should the narrow persistent Side Panel keep Watch/resource results primary while advanced rules/mappings/diagnostics remain powerful, accessible and performant?

| Surface / behavior | STEP-04 disposition |
| --- | --- |
| top-level destinations | Watch (default), Rules, Settings |
| Watch header | exact current tab/page identity + Watch/Stop primary CTA + readiness/permission/degraded state |
| default filters | compact Images / Videos controls |
| include/exclude globs | advanced disclosure under Watch; validate before Watch |
| live resource stream | **v0.0.21 implemented:** bounded first/older page queries, stable occurrence identity, shallow 500-row UI buffer and fixed-row virtual window; preserve selected resource detail |
| session/history selection | **v0.0.21 implemented:** contextual recent Watch-session picker using setup name/start time/live context; opaque IDs remain internal |
| Packagizer rules/templates | Rules destination with ordered list/editor |
| Token Browser | contextual to rule/template editor; source namespaces grouped and Missing-aware |
| Page Fields | contextual dependency surface under Rules/Preview, not a top-level app mode |
| Preview/Test | first-class Rules action using same semantic engines as live |
| permissions | contextual readiness/grant/retry/revoke flow; not navigation |
| diagnostics/support | **v0.0.26 implemented:** Settings summary first, contextual support guidance, structural/redacted technical disclosure second; no opaque-ID entry |
| retention/Clear/privacy | **v0.0.28 reconciled:** bounded terminal-history age/count controls + manual maintenance + approximate pressure status sit above unchanged explicit Clear scopes; active-Watch destructive guard and separate site-permission authority remain |
| keyboard | **v0.0.27 implemented:** semantic Watch / Rules / Settings tabs use roving focus; primary actions remain native controls; no drag-only or focus-trap path |
| focus/status | **v0.0.27 implemented:** 3px visible focus plus scroll margin; destructive-action focus restoration retained; one atomic polite summarized live lane plus alert semantics for errors |
| live announcements | **v0.0.27 reconciled:** one shared atomic polite announcement lane summarizes workspace state and meaningful result changes; row-by-row additions never create competing live regions |
| color | **v0.0.27 implemented:** canonical state text remains visible and live state also has a non-color marker; errors/warnings/state never rely on color alone |
| reflow | **v0.0.27 implemented:** explicit 320 CSS px one-column shell/action/editor reflow with DOM/task order unchanged and long resource text allowed to wrap |
| target sizing | **v0.0.27 implemented:** primary controls retain 2.75rem minimum height; checkbox target is 1.5rem and wrapped by the existing labeled row target |
| motion | **v0.0.27 implemented:** reduced-motion media query suppresses meaningful transitions/animations and forced smooth scrolling |
| localization | **v0.0.27 implemented:** complete English Side Panel catalog routes through Chrome i18n with deterministic English fallback; WXT `public/_locales/en/messages.json` and localized manifest placeholders are source-tested |
| live list state | **v0.0.21 implemented:** bounded page query + invalidation requery/merge + `shallowRef` row buffer; no complete-history component graph |
| streaming | one-shot query correctness + invalidation-only Port; reconnect re-queries bounded sessions/page/detail as needed; no streaming canonical cache |
| popup/devtools/options | popup/devtools rejected baseline; options deferred |

## Common Watch flow

1. Side Panel opens on **Watch** and shows exact tab/page plus readiness.
2. User chooses Images/Videos and optionally expands Advanced filters.
3. User invokes **Watch**; any missing optional host authority is requested from this gesture.
4. Watching state remains conspicuous with Stop and scope identity.
5. New admitted resources appear in a virtualized stream; summarized counts may be announced.
6. Selecting a resource shows source/derived facts and actions without leaving Watch.
7. Rules/Preview/Page Fields are edited separately and affect only future Watch sessions under frozen-definition constraints.

## STEP-03 query/projection disposition

- Existing IndexedDB v1 `watchSessions.byCreatedAt` and `resourceObservations.byWatchSessionObservedAt` indexes are sufficient for the current newest-first history experience; no new store/index is added.
- Default resource page 40, maximum page 100, bounded scan 500, recent sessions 20 and Side Panel row buffer 500 are current implementation constants, not final performance-certified thresholds.
- User-facing bounded search covers URL/filename/group and filters cover kind/status. Arbitrary grouping/sort is intentionally absent because the accepted query/index authority does not support a useful alternative without scope expansion.
- Same canonical URL occurrences remain separate rows. The list never destroys reversible occurrence/dedup provenance.
- Selected detail is human summary first; structural explanation is progressive, and raw sensitive payload/request/document/internal-rule identifiers are outside the normal contract.
- Separate monotonic freshness sequences protect sessions, pages and detail from stale out-of-order replacement.

## STEP-09 whole-product shell disposition

- Canonical presentation states are exactly `empty`, `loading`, `disabled`, `error`, `success`, `live`, `degraded`, `reconnecting`, and `stale`; domain/runtime enums remain unchanged and are humanized only at presentation boundaries.
- Static Side Panel copy is externalized through the English catalog and Chrome `i18n`; manifest name/description use `__MSG_*__`, and WXT's vanilla i18n layout is `public/_locales/en/messages.json`.
- One `role=status` / `aria-live=polite` / `aria-atomic=true` region owns summarized meaningful announcements. Error surfaces retain `role=alert`; ordinary notices do not create competing live regions.
- Semantic DOM order remains the task order at all widths. At 320 CSS px, tabs/actions/forms/editors reflow to one column without CSS visual-order reordering.
- Visible focus, scroll margin, non-drag ordering, target sizing, reduced motion and non-color state are mechanically source-tested.
- STEP-09 changes presentation/localization only: durable domain repositories, control-plane query authority, invalidation-only Ports, permission scope, IndexedDB schema and runtime semantics are unchanged.

## STEP-10 durability-state disposition

- Settings presents bounded retention policy and an explicitly approximate storage estimate rather than exact remaining-capacity claims.
- Critical storage pressure maps to the shared `degraded` presentation state; maintenance outcomes use the existing summarized status lane.
- A durable observation-write failure ends Watch with human-facing `storage_failure` recovery language rather than leaving the shell in `live`.
- Restart reconciliation hydrates/requeries through the existing one-shot control-plane authority; no new UI cache or presentation durability tier is introduced.
- STEP-10 does not change the STEP-09 localization/accessibility shell contract; repeated churn/accessibility/capacity testing remains STEP-12.

## STEP-12 measured hardening disposition

- 10,000-row history/merge workloads confirm the current bounded page/scan/buffer architecture without promoting those constants to product maxima.
- The Side Panel now coalesces burst invalidation hints into one 50ms refresh wave. Each wave still performs authoritative one-shot hydration/resource queries; Ports remain non-canonical hints.
- A 100,000-logical-row virtual-window workload keeps the mounted set bounded by viewport + overscan, and the final dynamic-list source contract preserves focusability, selected-row semantics, the single summarized live region, 320px reflow, visible focus and reduced motion.
- 100 reconnect cycles reject stale disconnected-port hints, and repeated durable-write recovery tests preserve exactly one durable observation per terminal request.
- Timing budgets in `performance-readiness.json` are local regression guards only. No SLA or product maximum is certified.
- Origin-backed Chromium IndexedDB measurement is `deferred_environment` because the current headless/CDP context denies IndexedDB access; packaged extension-host/assistive-technology proof remains STEP-13/14.

## Recommendation

Use progressive disclosure and a single narrow-pane task hierarchy. Do not mirror the domain model as many top-level tabs.

## Review / disposition

Accepted as the Side Panel IA/performance contract and revised through v0.0.28. STEP-09 closes the feature-complete shell/state/reflow/accessibility/localization baseline; STEP-10 reconciles real durability outcomes into that grammar; v0.0.30 STEP-12 closes measured capacity/repeated-churn accessibility hardening; final packaged assistive-technology and release-candidate certification remain STEP-13/14 work.

## Revision history

| Date | Revision | Change | Status |
| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
| 2026-08-19 | 1 | Define Watch-first IA, accessibility, localization and large-list performance dispositions | active |
| 2026-08-20 | 2 | Record v0.0.21 bounded/index-driven resource paging, virtual rows, human session context, summarized live updates and redacted detail | active |
| 2026-08-20 | 3 | Record v0.0.26 typed Settings, explicit safe Clear scopes, privacy/redacted diagnostics, support guidance and focus/status restoration | active |
| 2026-08-20 | 4 | Record v0.0.27 canonical state grammar, summarized live announcements, WXT/Chrome localization baseline, 320px reflow, visible focus, target sizing, reduced motion and non-color presentation | active |
| 2026-08-20 | 5 | Reconcile v0.0.28 bounded retention, approximate pressure, storage-failure termination and restart outcomes into the existing state/status/control-plane grammar | active |
| 2026-08-20 | 6 | Record v0.0.30 measured bounded-history/virtualization, invalidation batching, reconnect/recovery churn and dynamic-list accessibility evidence | active |
</file>

