# MATRIX-0014 - Wave-1 Consolidated Architecture and Wave-2 Scope

## Objective

Collapse ROADMAP-0001 STEP-01 through STEP-04 into one internally consistent implementation denominator and distinguish required Wave-2 work from later enhancements, explicit deferrals and rejected patterns.

## Consolidated disposition matrix

| Capability / contract | Disposition | Wave-2 status | Accepted denominator |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Explicit user Watch boundary | retain | required | tab-scoped; no ambient idle collection; no silent browser-restart resume |
| Passive `webRequest` observation | adopt | required | baseline network authority; non-blocking |
| Optional broad HTTP(S) host authority | adopt | required | requested from Watch flow; denial/revocation visible |
| `activeTab` as comprehensive capture | reject | negative scope | insufficient for arbitrary third-party resources |
| `chrome.debugger`/CDP baseline | defer | later advanced | separate permission/security UX only if future need proves it |
| Resource Timing/DOM signals | adapt | supplemental | non-canonical enrichment/evidence only |
| Payload/body/cookie/credential capture | reject | negative scope | metadata-minimized baseline |
| Immutable ResourceObservation history | retain | required | WatchSession + request identity; no destructive rewrite |
| URL duplicate folding | adopt | required projection | reversible within accepted session/document scope |
| semantic image/video/stream classification | adopt | required | explicit MIME/type/path evidence and reason; generic media not automatically video |
| Images/Videos presets | adopt | required | Images=image; Videos=video+stream_manifest |
| minimal URL glob v1 | adopt | required | full canonical URL no fragment; `*`/`?`/escapes only |
| ordered declarative Packagizer | adopt | required | immutable condition source; derived actions; stop-after-success |
| same evaluator for Preview/live | retain | required | one semantic engine with structural/redacted explanation |
| Missing distinct from falsey/empty | retain | required | explicit default/error handling |
| arbitrary JS/eval/sensitive token namespaces | reject | negative scope | no executable user code or credential/body tokens |
| regex rule language | defer | later | add only with bounded syntax/performance/security evidence |
| rule import/export format | defer | later | useful, not required to deliver baseline product |
| exact-document PageContext | adopt | required | WatchSession + tab + topDocumentId + pageRevision |
| exact-document on-demand scripting | adopt | required | isolated world; returned identity verified |
| typed CSS/XPath/read/cardinality/fallback | adopt | required | snapshot/scalar semantics; fail closed on errors |
| referenced PageFieldMapping freeze | adopt | required | only enabled referenced definitions enter Watch snapshot |
| ambient continuous DOM scraping | reject baseline | negative/later | no hidden MutationObserver authority |
| subframe mapping editor | defer | later | top-level document baseline |
| MV3 + Chrome 116+ + WXT + Vue 3 + TS | adopt | required family | exact pins refreshed and locked in STEP-01 |
| Side Panel as canonical state | reject | negative scope | presentation/query/command projection only |
| IndexedDB durable local authority | adopt | required | revisioned definitions/sessions/observations/enrichment/projection/meta |
| exact physical IndexedDB topology | defer to implementation | required decision | STEP-03 selects/version-tests v1 topology under logical boundaries |
| storage.session active coordination | adopt | required | survives worker stop; clears browser restart |
| storage.local small preferences | adopt | required | not history authority |
| storage.sync / unlimitedStorage baseline | reject | negative scope | bounded local retention/quota UX first |
| versioned object/message/migration authority | adopt | required | stable IDs/revisions/schema/protocol versions from first durable scaffold |
| Watch / Rules / Settings IA | adopt | required | Watch default; advanced capabilities contextual |
| virtualized/windowed resource stream | adopt | required | bounded hydration + append deltas + shallow presentation rows |
| accessibility/localization/reduced motion | adopt | required | implementation-entry acceptance, not release polish |
| local redacted diagnostics | adopt | required | no raw sensitive browsing values persisted by default |
| remote telemetry/upload | reject baseline | negative scope | local-only unless future explicit product/security scope |
| popup/DevTools as primary product UI | reject baseline | negative scope | Side Panel is primary surface |

## Required Wave-2 closure families

1. reproducible extension/toolchain/runtime and versioned contract foundation;
2. local durable persistence, immutable definition/session authority and migration basis;
3. optional-host Watch lifecycle and raw network observation;
4. resource classification/dedup/admission and declarative Packagizer/Preview;
5. exact-document PageContext/PageField enrichment;
6. Side Panel hydration, Watch/Rules/Settings product composition and large-list behavior;
7. retention/quota/restart recovery, security/privacy/accessibility/performance integration;
8. build/package/install/upgrade/store-readiness, cold recovery and final release-candidate certification.

## Later / rejected scope preserved

Debugger/CDP capture, regex, rule import/export, historical bulk re-evaluation, downloader control, ambient continuous DOM scraping, baseline subframe editor UX, `unlimitedStorage`, `storage.sync` history, remote telemetry/upload, arbitrary user JS/plugins and sensitive payload/token capture are not unexplained missing work.

## Recommendation

Accept ADR-0001 through ADR-0005 as the Wave-2 denominator and require ROADMAP-0002 to trace every step to this matrix or an explicit integration/security/migration/performance/package/recovery closure need.
</file>

