## Shared state contract

| State | Visible label pattern | Announcement/focus behavior |
| --- | --- | --- |
| empty | `No <items> yet` + next action | no focus move |
| loading | `Loading…` | polite status if meaningful |
| disabled | disabled control + textual reason | no color-only meaning |
| success | `Saved`, `Updated`, `Access granted` | polite status; retain focus unless workflow moves logically |
| live | `Watching` + Stop | persistent non-color state |
| reconnecting | `Reconnecting…` | preserve bounded view; rehydrate after reconnect |
| stale | `Page changed` / `Saved item changed elsewhere` | block unsafe publish/test; preserve working copy |
| degraded | `Limited operation — <reason>` | show safe available actions |
| error | action-specific human message | submitted invalid form may focus first invalid field; background errors do not steal focus |

## Picker, ordering and responsive contract

- Native `select` is the baseline; `optgroup` only for meaningful grouping.
- Searchable custom combobox requires demonstrated scale need and full keyboard/focus/name/value/popup tests; no arbitrary item threshold is invented.
- Move up/down is mandatory for every reorderable list; drag cannot be the only pointer operation.
- Narrow one-column semantic DOM order is canonical. Wider presentation may group visually without changing task/read/focus order.
- Normal content targets 320 CSS px-equivalent reflow without page-level two-dimensional scrolling.
- Custom/frequent targets meet at least the WCAG 2.2 AA 24 CSS px size/spacing baseline.

## Current-domain UI test/harness selection

When STEP-02 first changes executable UI:

1. add one shared Side Panel UI contract harness around the real Vue App/shared components with typed stub clients;
2. assert user vocabulary, dirty/saved/conflict state, disabled reasons, command intent, tab/disclosure keyboard semantics, focus restoration, passive status roles and narrow semantic order;
3. keep domain semantics in existing Watch/resource/Packagizer/Page Field/definition tests rather than duplicating them in UI fixtures;
4. extend the same harness across STEP-03–09 instead of adding historical per-step UI suites;
5. classify unavailable real-browser/AT lanes as `deferred_environment`, never synthetic passes.

## Review / disposition

Accepted as ROADMAP-0003 interaction/ownership authority and revised through STEP-12. Phases P1–P5 are closed with repository-controlled durability, browser security/privacy, performance/capacity/accessibility/localization and failure-recovery hardening. STEP-13 build/package/install/upgrade/store-readiness certification is the only next owner.

