<file path="agents/records/README.md">
# Durable Records

`agents/records/` contains managed project authority and durable evidence.

Supported record families include:

- `ADR` - architectural or durable technical decisions;
- `AUDIT` - bounded readiness/compliance/evidence assessments;
- `CONSTRAINT` - active restrictions or non-negotiable boundaries;
- `DEFERRAL` - explicitly postponed work with a revisit trigger;
- `FINDING` - bounded verified facts with repository implications;
- `ISSUE` - durable tracked problems when a record is useful;
- `MATRIX` - comparison or coverage evidence;
- `REFERENCE` - governed pointers to external/internal source material;
- `ROADMAP` - coordinated multi-step delivery plans.

The starter baseline contains no inherited project records. The first roadmap created by a target project is therefore `ROADMAP-0001`.

`roadmaps/README.md` exists only to preserve the empty topic directory in archives and repositories.

## Helper

`python3 agents/scripts/record-manager.py` may validate record envelopes, allocate the next visible stable ID, and render canonical record templates. It does not maintain a registry outside the repository and cannot accept or close records automatically.
</file>

