# REFERENCE-0007 - URL MIME and User Glob Standards Authority

## Purpose

Preserve current first-party standards/API authority needed to define deterministic URL identity, resource classification and a small user-facing glob language without confusing that language with Chrome permission match patterns.

## Referenced material

- WHATWG URL Standard: https://url.spec.whatwg.org/
- WHATWG MIME Sniffing Standard: https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/
- IANA Media Types registry: https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/media-types.xhtml
- Chrome content-script glob documentation: https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/reference/manifest/content-scripts
- Chrome match patterns: https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/develop/concepts/match-patterns
- Chrome `webRequest`: https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/reference/api/webRequest

## Current facts retained for STEP-02

- `webRequest.requestId` is stable for one logical request lifecycle, while redirects/authentication can map several physical HTTP requests to the same web request.
- WHATWG URL parsing/serialization provides the normalization denominator; fragment exclusion is available without mutating query data.
- MIME essence and MIME groups provide higher-quality classification evidence than filename extension alone. IANA registers `application/vnd.apple.mpegurl` for HLS and `application/dash+xml` for DASH.
- Chrome `ResourceType` describes usage. Its generic `media` value cannot be interpreted as "video" without additional evidence.
- Chrome `include_globs`/`exclude_globs` establish a useful `*`/`?` wildcard precedent, while Chrome host/permission match patterns are a separate structured grammar.

## Provenance

Primary standards/API pages refreshed 2026-08-19 for ROADMAP-0001 STEP-02. Detailed source-fact/interpretation separation is in `agents/records/research-data/20260819/20260819T104500Z_v0002_step02-resource-filter-packagizer-token-preview-authority.md`.

## Usage constraints

This record is source authority, not an implementation ADR. crsniffer deliberately does not perform body-based MIME sniffing in the baseline because CONSTRAINT-0003 excludes response-body capture.

## Related records

FINDING-0011 through FINDING-0013, MATRIX-0005, MATRIX-0006, ROADMAP-0001 STEP-02/STEP-05.

