# REFERENCE-0009 - Current DOM XPath and Page-Text Standards Authority

## Purpose

Preserve current primary standards authority for CSS selector snapshots, attribute absence, XPath result typing/snapshot behavior, rendered-text semantics, and markup serialization decisions used by STEP-03 page-field research.

## Referenced material

- WHATWG DOM Standard: https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/
- W3C DOM Level 3 XPath: https://www.w3.org/TR/DOM-Level-3-XPath/
- WHATWG HTML `innerText` / `outerText`: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#the-innertext-idl-attribute
- WHATWG HTML dynamic markup insertion / `innerHTML` / `outerHTML`: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dynamic-markup-insertion.html

## Current facts retained for STEP-03

- DOM `querySelectorAll()` returns a static result rather than a live collection.
- DOM `getAttribute()` returns null when the requested attribute is absent, which must not be collapsed into empty string.
- XPath evaluation is contextual and can produce string, number, boolean, single-node, iterator, or snapshot node-set result forms.
- XPath ordered node iterators can be invalidated by document mutation; ordered node snapshots remain iterable after mutation, while reevaluation can still yield different nodes.
- HTML `innerText` represents rendered text semantics and differs from raw descendant `textContent` behavior.
- `innerHTML` and `outerHTML` serialize markup, materially expanding content/sensitivity/size compared with text/attribute/scalar reads.

## Provenance

Primary specifications retrieved/refreshed 2026-08-19. The XPath specification is an older stable W3C DOM API specification; STEP-03 uses it only for browser API result-model facts corroborated by current Chromium/donor behavior, not as freshness authority for unrelated modern platform behavior.

## Usage constraints

This reference establishes platform semantics, not crsniffer architecture. STEP-03 matrices decide which result/read forms are admitted into the baseline. Markup reads are researched but deferred for privacy/product-scope reasons.

## Related records

