# REFERENCE-0012 - Current Chrome Side Panel Persistence Accessibility and Store Authority

## Purpose

Record current Chrome/W3C authority for Side Panel behavior, storage tiers, MV3 lifecycle, accessibility/reflow/status behavior and Chrome Web Store trust constraints used by STEP-04.

## Referenced material

Current first-party documentation refreshed 2026-08-19 establishes:

- Chrome Side Panel is an MV3 extension page available from Chrome 114; `sidePanel.open()` is available from Chrome 116 and requires user interaction. A Side Panel can remain open alongside browsing and access extension APIs.
- `chrome.storage.session` is memory-backed, survives service-worker shutdown but is cleared on browser restart/extension reload/update; `storage.local` is durable and quota-bounded; `storage.sync` is small and unsuitable for high-volume observation history.
- IndexedDB is available to extension service workers and persists under the extension origin; extension storage is not cleared with ordinary browsing-data deletion, so the product must provide its own explicit retention/clear controls.
- MV3 service workers can terminate after inactivity. Long-lived messaging may support streaming but must not be a correctness requirement.
- Chrome extension accessibility guidance favors native semantic controls, complete keyboard navigation and visible focus. WCAG 2.2 provides reflow, focus visibility, target-size and status-message guidance applicable to a narrow persistent Side Panel.
- Chrome Web Store policy requires a narrow understandable purpose, accurate disclosure and browsing-data collection limited to what the prominently described feature needs.

## Provenance

Official Chrome Extensions / Chrome Web Store documentation and W3C WCAG 2.2 guidance current at STEP-04 research time.

## Usage constraints

Storage quotas and exact API details must be rechecked during implementation. STEP-04 defines ownership/policy, not physical object-store schemas, migration code, quota thresholds or final retention durations.

