# REFERENCE-0014 — ROADMAP-0003 STEP-01 current Chrome/WAI and Crscraper UI/UX authority

## Reference scope

Freeze the current external and read-only donor authority used to close ROADMAP-0003 STEP-01 without turning transient web research into chat-only evidence.

## Current first-party sources

### Chrome Extensions

- Side Panel API: `https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/reference/api/sidePanel`
- Permissions API: `https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/reference/api/permissions`
- Declare permissions: `https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/develop/concepts/declare-permissions`
- Scripting API: `https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/reference/api/scripting`
- i18n API: `https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/reference/api/i18n`
- Tabs API: `https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/reference/api/tabs`

Accepted source facts:

- optional permission requests are user-gesture gated;
- active-tab identity is available from `tabs.query`, while sensitive tab properties such as URL/title require the `tabs` permission or matching host authority; STEP-02 therefore keeps exact address display permission-contextual rather than adding `tabs`;
- scripting requires `scripting` plus host authority and defaults to `ISOLATED` execution world;
- Side Panel is an extension-page surface intended to accompany browsing context;
- Chrome i18n externalizes user-visible strings through `_locales` message catalogs.

### W3C WAI / WCAG 2.2

- ARIA APG Tabs: `https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/tabs/`
- ARIA APG Combobox: `https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/combobox/`
- WCAG 2.2 Dragging Movements: `https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/dragging-movements`
- WCAG 2.2 Target Size (Minimum): `https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/target-size-minimum`
- WCAG 2.2 Reflow: `https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/reflow`
- WCAG 2.2 Status Messages: `https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/status-messages.html`

Accepted source facts:

- APG tabs have composite keyboard semantics; manual activation is a valid pattern;
- custom comboboxes carry non-trivial keyboard/focus/value/popup obligations;
- a drag interaction needs an equivalent single-pointer non-drag path under WCAG 2.2 AA unless essential;
- WCAG 2.2 AA target-size baseline is 24 CSS px subject to defined exceptions/spacing;
- normal content must support 320 CSS px-equivalent reflow without two-dimensional page scrolling where not inherently two-dimensional;
- passive progress/result/error status must be programmatically exposed without requiring focus movement.

## Read-only donor authority

Promoted `crscraper v0.0.45` was inspected from the user's Library. Material records:

- `ROADMAP-0004--whole-product-ui-ux-recovery-donor-parity-and-chrome-native-enhancement.md`
