# REFERENCE-0015 — ROADMAP-0003 STEP-03 bounded resource history and status authority

## Reference scope

Freeze the current first-party and read-only donor facts used to implement ROADMAP-0003 STEP-03 without turning external research into chat-only evidence.

## Current first-party sources

### Chrome Extensions

- Side Panel API: `https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/reference/api/sidePanel`
- Messaging concepts: `https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/develop/concepts/messaging`

Accepted disposition:

- keep resource browsing/detail inside the Side Panel companion surface;
- use bounded one-shot request/response queries for correctness;
- keep the existing long-lived Port as invalidation/reconnect transport only;
- do not add a Chrome permission for resource-history presentation.

### IndexedDB 3.0

- W3C IndexedDB 3.0: `https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB-3/`

Accepted disposition:

- use existing ordered indexes/cursors rather than full-store materialization;
- resume resource history through the exact index-key/primary-key cursor position with `continuePrimaryKey`;
- preserve physical IndexedDB version 1 and the existing store/index topology.

### WAI / WCAG 2.2

- Status Messages: `https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/status-messages.html`

Accepted disposition:

- live result additions use summarized passive status announcements without stealing focus;
- selecting/detail inspection remains an explicit user action rather than an automatic focus change.

## Read-only donor disposition

Promoted `crscraper v0.0.45` ROADMAP-0004 STEP-11 supports adopting task-facing result search/filter/list/detail, progressive technical detail and ordinary inspection without opaque IDs. Crsniffer adapts those principles to immutable WatchSession/resource-occurrence history and rejects scraper-specific Run/Record/export/recovery concepts.

## Repository implication

STEP-03 may add a bounded query/projection service and Side Panel virtualized result experience over existing persisted authority. It does not authorize a new persistence store, new permission, streaming canonical cache, destructive deduplication or later Rules/Page Fields/Settings work.

Initial page/scan/buffer thresholds are implementation constants and not final capacity certification; ROADMAP-0003 STEP-12 owns later measured tuning/hardening.

## Review / freshness

Recheck IndexedDB/browser/UI authority if later work changes ordering/index strategy, live transport correctness, custom widgets or the permission surface.

