# REFERENCE-0016 — ROADMAP-0003 STEP-06 Page Field authoring and exact-page assist authority

## Reference scope

Freeze the current first-party browser/accessibility and read-only donor evidence used to implement ROADMAP-0003 STEP-06 without widening Crsniffer's accepted permission or document-attribution model.

## Current first-party authority

### Chrome Extensions

- Scripting API: `https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/reference/api/scripting`
- Declare permissions: `https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/develop/concepts/declare-permissions`
- Permissions API: `https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/reference/api/permissions`

Accepted disposition:

- reuse existing `scripting` + optional HTTP/HTTPS host authority; do not add `activeTab`, `tabs`, required/broader hosts, debugger/CDP or MAIN-world execution;
- target the exact attributed `documentId` and explicit `ISOLATED` world for Page Field DOM assistance;
- verify the returned injection document identity and re-check current WatchSession/tab/document/pageRevision before accepting Test/Highlight/Pick results;
- keep optional host authority user-mediated and make page assistance unavailable when exact PageContext/host authority is unavailable.

### W3C WAI / WCAG 2.2

- Focus Appearance: `https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/focus-appearance.html`
- Status Messages: `https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/status-messages.html`
- Dragging Movements: `https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/dragging-movements.html`

Accepted disposition:

- page-assist commands remain explicit keyboard-focusable buttons with the existing focus-visible treatment;
- completion/failure uses passive status/error semantics instead of moving focus;
- fallback and transform order always has Move up/Move down alternatives and never depends on drag.

## Read-only donor disposition

Then-latest promoted `crscraper v0.0.50` was inspected from the user's Library (bundle SHA-256 `805d3d149d4d4350ba97c241f559415e681998a3d28d0898758de2a055509a9d`). Its retained structured Mapping editor supports adopting ordered field/fallback rows, progressive advanced mapping controls and non-drag ordering. Crsniffer adapts only those interaction principles to its existing CSS/XPath PageFieldMapping schema and exact-document authority; no donor code, scraper Setup/Traversal domains, persistence or permission assumptions are copied.

## Repository implication

STEP-06 may add structured Page Field working-copy/publish/query services and explicit bounded Test/Highlight/Pick helpers over existing saved definitions, PageContextRegistry, PageFieldEvaluationService and Chrome scripting authority. It does not authorize a new persistence store, durable authoring history, ambient DOM observer, new permission, generic import/export/lifecycle work or runtime semantic expansion.

## Review / freshness

Recheck this authority if later work adds a new Chrome permission, content-script/world model, continuous page observation, custom complex widgets or broader page-assistance behavior.

