# REFERENCE-0021 — ROADMAP-0003 STEP-13 Build Package Store and Native Theme Authority

## Purpose

Record the v0.0.31 release-boundary authority used to distinguish repository correctness from unavailable native package/browser infrastructure and to define the supported Chrome-native-aware appearance contract.

## Release environment rule

`agents/governance/environment-deferrals.md` is normative: missing external/tooling capability is non-blocking when repository-owned work can be completed correctly. STEP-13 therefore records selected lock/WXT/generated-extension install/update/Web Store evidence as `deferred_environment` in this environment rather than converting it into a package defect or a roadmap block.

Repository defects remain blocking: incorrect version/package pins, permission/CSP drift, missing locale/store/privacy docs, broken migrations, non-deterministic recovery, failing executable tests or a contradictory authority record cannot be relabeled as environment deferrals.

## Native theme authority

Crsniffer may use public web-platform/native mechanisms available to extension pages: system font stack, `color-scheme`, CSS system colors, native semantic form controls, automatic control accent, selection colors, `prefers-contrast` and `forced-colors` handling.

Crsniffer must not claim a supported bridge to Chrome's private arbitrary toolbar/tab/omnibox/WebUI theme-token palette. Exact custom Chrome theme hue synchronization is outside the public extension-page contract. The product should look at home across light/dark/high-contrast modes without copying private `chrome://` styling or freezing current Chrome palette values.

## Package/store authority

- package versions remain exact source pins;
- manifest required permissions remain `storage`, `webRequest`, `webNavigation`, `scripting`;
- HTTP/HTTPS host access remains optional/user-mediated;
- incognito remains disabled and extension CSP remains self-only;
- Chrome i18n English baseline remains packaged under `public/_locales/en/messages.json`;
- physical IndexedDB remains v1 and logical schema remains v2;
- legacy persisted upgrade semantics remain repository-tested;
- no telemetry/upload, remote code or new permission is introduced for store readiness;
- deterministic source/recovery identity is certified locally; native WXT package/install/update/Web Store evidence is deferred when unavailable.

## Usage constraints

A future capable environment should resolve the selected dependency/package deferral in place. It must not change product semantics merely to make the environment convenient and must not rewrite v0.0.31 as if native package evidence ran here.

