- IndexedDB is available to extension service workers for structured durable state.
- `storage.local` is durable/quota-bounded; `storage.sync` is small and inappropriate for high-volume history.
- Extension-origin persisted data needs product retention/Clear controls; normal browsing-data deletion is not a substitute.

## Accessibility/store facts

- Native semantic controls, keyboard operation and visible focus remain first-choice Chrome extension accessibility guidance.
- WCAG 2.2 supplies reflow/focus/status/target-size criteria relevant to the narrow Side Panel.
- Live resource-row additions are result changes; announce Watch/error/progress and summarized count changes rather than every row.
- Chrome Web Store policy requires narrow disclosed purpose and limits browsing-activity collection to the prominently described user-facing feature.

## crsniffer interpretation

Preferred denominator entering STEP-05: MV3 + Chrome 116+ + WXT + Vue 3 + TypeScript + Side Panel. Side Panel is presentation/command plane, not durable authority. Candidate local state tiers are IndexedDB durable domain state, storage.session browser-lifetime active coordination, and storage.local small preferences. Long-lived Ports are optional streaming optimizations only.

The primary navigation hierarchy is Watch / Rules / Settings. Watch remains default with exact scope/status, Watch/Stop, Images/Videos, advanced globs and a virtualized resource stream. Rules own ordered rules/templates/token browser/Preview and contextual Page Fields. Settings owns retention/Clear/privacy/support/diagnostics. Permission grant/retry/revoke is contextual rather than navigation.

