# ROADMAP-0001 - Crsniffer Research-First Architecture and Successor Planning

## Executive summary

`crsniffer` opens as a five-step research-first Wave 1. The product intent is clear - Watch-led Chrome network resource observation, image/video plus glob filtering, Packagizer-like rule/template behavior, and page-aware XPath-derived token fields - but the capture engine, permission model, observation/rule/token contracts, document lifecycle, persistence, stack, and frontend architecture are not yet proven.

The repository therefore spends four promoted iterations on bounded research/synthesis inputs and a fifth on architecture synthesis plus creation of a separate implementation/stabilization roadmap. ROADMAP-0001 authorizes no production extension/runtime implementation.

`v0.0.0` is the roadmap-opening/governance iteration and is not STEP-01. Planned Wave-1 promoted execution is `v0.0.1` through `v0.0.5`.

## Problem statement

A network sniffer is permission- and lifecycle-sensitive in ways that a page scraper is not. Third-party CDN/media resource visibility, Chrome host authority, MV3 service-worker interruption, page/document identity, resource dedup/classification, rule/template determinism, page field freshness, privacy/retention, and Side Panel ergonomics all affect durable/public contracts. Implementing first would make the most expensive decisions least informed.

## Goals

- Determine a defensible Chrome network-observation architecture and Watch lifecycle.
- Define resource observation, filter/glob, Packagizer rule/token/template, and preview semantics.
- Define document-aware XPath field mapping that can safely enrich resource token contexts.
- Select the application stack, persistence, frontend/Side Panel architecture, accessibility/performance/privacy and diagnostics policies from current evidence.
- Synthesize accepted contracts and create an evidence-derived successor ROADMAP-0002 before development begins.

## Non-goals

- Production extension/runtime implementation during v0.0.1-v0.0.5.
- Copying Cat Catch or crscraper runtime code/permission architecture.
