# Phase P1 - Runtime, Contracts, Persistence, and Immutable Watch Authority

### STEP-01 - Extension Toolchain, Manifest, Side Panel, and Reproducible Build Shell
**Target:** `v0.0.6`
**Purpose:** Fresh-check and lock exact Chrome 116+ / WXT / Vue 3 / TypeScript / runtime/package-manager versions; create the smallest buildable MV3 Side Panel/background shell and generated-manifest authority.
**Depends on:** ROADMAP-0001 complete.
**Evidence:** ADR-0004, ADR-0005, MATRIX-0014.

Acceptance: exact runtime/package pins and install/build/typecheck/package commands committed; minimal MV3 background + Side Panel source shell and generated-manifest authority committed; manifest/CSP/permission floor kept minimal; no Watch semantics yet. Registry hydration, trustworthy transitive `package-lock.json`, `wxt prepare`, typecheck/build/package execution may be `deferred_environment` under fast path. The P1 checkpoint must attempt this lane; an environment-only failure may carry into P2 but must be resolved in the first capable environment and before STEP-20 package/release certification.

STEP-01 fast-path result: selected Node 24.19.0/npm 11.17.0, WXT 0.21.3, Vue 3.5.41, `@wxt-dev/module-vue` 1.0.3, TypeScript 7.0.2 and `vue-tsc` 3.3.9; committed exact pins plus `.nvmrc`/`.npmrc`/WXT config/background/Side Panel shell. Current container Node/npm are 22.16.0/10.9.2. The v0.0.9 P1 checkpoint retried npm-registry access and timed out, so hydrated lockfile/typecheck/build/package remain explicit `deferred_environment`; they do not block early P2 implementation but must be resolved before STEP-20 package/release certification.

### STEP-02 - Core IDs, JSON-Safe Contracts, Missing, Errors, and Message Envelopes
**Target:** `v0.0.7`
**Purpose:** Implement stable IDs/revisions/schema/protocol versions, Missing, typed errors and cross-context envelopes before durable/user-visible state depends on them.
**Evidence:** ADR-0002, ADR-0003, ADR-0004, FINDING-0031.

STEP-02 fast-path result: added dependency-free `src/core/` authority for canonical project-owned UUID-v4 IDs, positive safe-integer revisions and separate logical/message/error schema versions, strict JSON values that reject silent JSON coercion/omission, explicit Missing wire encoding, bounded typed errors, and frozen versioned request/response envelopes with WatchSession/tab/document context. Focused validation passed the standalone core TypeScript check and 8/8 Node contract tests. The iteration-start donor check advanced to promoted crscraper v0.0.39; its STEP-05 changes are performance/persistence-query hardening only and do not change this contract denominator. STEP-01 registry hydration/build proof remains deferred_environment until the P1 checkpoint.

### STEP-03 - IndexedDB v1, Storage Tiers, Repositories, and Migration Authority
**Target:** `v0.0.8`
**Purpose:** Select and implement tested physical IndexedDB v1 topology under the accepted logical authorities; integrate `storage.session` and `storage.local`; establish physical/logical migration separation.
**Evidence:** ADR-0004, MATRIX-0012, FINDING-0031.

STEP-03 fast-path result: implemented physical IndexedDB v1 with five typed authority stores (`meta`, `definitions`, `watchSessions`, `resourceObservations`, `pageFieldSnapshots`), bounded query indexes, strict JSON-safe repositories, `storage.session`/`storage.local` namespace adapters, and resumable post-open logical migration checkpoints distinct from short exclusive physical `versionchange` upgrades. The manifest now declares only the required `storage` permission; no host/capture permission was pulled forward. Focused validation passed core+persistence TypeScript checks, 14/14 directly dependent core+persistence tests, and the storage-permission static assertion. The iteration-start donor remains promoted crscraper v0.0.39; its stable IndexedDB-v1 hardening reinforces physical/logical version separation without changing crsniffer topology. Packaged extension-origin IndexedDB execution remains coupled to the inherited registry/build lane and is carried as `deferred_environment` until the first capable environment.

### STEP-04 - Saved Definitions, Revisions, and Immutable WatchSession Composition
**Target:** `v0.0.9`
**Purpose:** Implement mutable reusable Watch/filter/rule/template/PageField definitions plus immutable effective WatchSession snapshots/digests.
**Evidence:** ADR-0002, ADR-0003, ADR-0004, CONSTRAINT-0004, CONSTRAINT-0005.

STEP-04 fast-path result: added five revisioned reusable definition kinds (`watch`, `resourceFilter`, `packagizerRule`, `template`, `pageFieldMapping`) over the existing durable definitions store, optimistic revision updates, constrained reference composition, exact-revision dependency checks, canonical SHA-256 content digests, and immutable WatchSession snapshots. Watch freezes its referenced filter/rule/template definitions, including disabled definitions as historical configuration facts; dependencies of disabled definitions are not traversed. PageFieldMappings enter the session only through enabled frozen rule/template dependency paths, so unrelated mappings remain editable. Later definition edits create new revisions and new session digests without rewriting previous sessions. Focused STEP-04 validation passed 9/9 definition/session tests and the definitions TypeScript check.

## Phase P1 success criteria

- Buildable/testable MV3 shell exists with reproducible dependency authority.
- Versioned contracts and persistence exist before feature-rich UI/state.
- Watch start can freeze exact definition revisions without yet requiring live capture.
- The P1 checkpoint must attempt the STEP-01 registry/package lane. Environment-only failure may be carried as explicit `deferred_environment` into P2, but must be resolved in the first capable environment and before STEP-20 package/release certification.

## Phase P1 fast-path checkpoint - v0.0.9

**Status:** implementation complete with explicit environment deferral.

- Accumulated TypeScript checks passed for core, persistence and definitions.
- Accumulated focused tests passed **23/23**: core 8/8, persistence 6/6, definitions/session composition 9/9.
- Chrome 116 minimum and the current `storage` permission floor remain unchanged.
- The npm-registry checkpoint probe timed out in this container (`timeout` status 124), so trustworthy transitive `package-lock.json`, WXT prepare/typecheck/build/package, and packaged extension-origin IndexedDB execution remain `deferred_environment`.
- Under `agents/governance/fast-path.yaml`, this environment-only lane does not block P2 development. It must be rerun in the first capable environment and becomes blocking no later than STEP-20 package/release certification.
- No cold recovery, deterministic ZIP, full governance sweep, or Library publication is required for this phase checkpoint.

# Phase P2 - Watch, Network Observation, Resource Admission, and Packagizer

### STEP-05 - Optional Host Permission UX, Watch Lifecycle, and Runtime Readiness
**Target:** `v0.0.10`
**Purpose:** Implement explicit Watch/Stop state machine, optional HTTP(S) host request/revoke/denial/incomplete-coverage handling, tab-close/permission-loss termination and browser-restart non-resume.
**Evidence:** ADR-0001, CONSTRAINT-0003, MATRIX-0003/0004.

STEP-05 fast-path result: implemented optional HTTP(S) host authority as `optional_host_permissions` while keeping the install-time permission floor unchanged at `storage`; the Side Panel requests host authority only from the explicit Watch button gesture and re-verifies complete HTTP+HTTPS coverage before background start. Added one-active-Watch lifecycle authority with immutable WatchSession composition, separately mutable lifecycle history in IndexedDB `meta`, browser-lifetime active coordination in `chrome.storage.session`, target validation, default Watch bootstrap, current-version request/response routing, Stop, tab-close termination, permission-loss termination, and service-worker reconciliation without browser/runtime-restart silent resume. Incognito and non-HTTP(S) targets fail closed in the baseline. Focused validation passed the standalone Watch TypeScript lane, 12/12 Watch lifecycle/permission tests, and targeted manifest/background/panel assertions. No `webRequest` listener or ResourceObservation creation was introduced; those remain STEP-06.

### STEP-06 - webRequest Observation Lifecycle and Immutable ResourceObservation
**Target:** `v0.0.11`
**Purpose:** Implement passive network event aggregation, redirect/auth lifecycle, request identity and immutable payload-minimized observations.
**Evidence:** ADR-0001, ADR-0002, MATRIX-0005.

STEP-06 fast-path result: added required `webRequest` API authority while retaining HTTP/HTTPS only as STEP-05 optional host authority; capture listeners are registered only for the active Watch `tabId`. Added browser-session pending request traces with preassigned ResourceObservation IDs, service-worker restart/replay safety, ordered redirect and 401/407 authentication-challenge facts under one Chrome request ID, terminal completion/error/out-of-scope-redirect persistence, and payload-minimized MIME extraction from Content-Type only. No request body, form data, cookie/credential header, complete header-set, IP, WebSocket-message, blocking interception, auth-provider or debugger authority was introduced. Focused validation passed strict observation TypeScript, 12/12 observation lifecycle/capture tests, 12/12 directly dependent Watch tests, targeted manifest/runtime assertions, and the pre-documentation diff check. Classification, canonical URL/dedup and admission remain STEP-07.

### STEP-07 - Resource Classification, Canonical URL, Dedup Projection, and Admission Filtering
**Target:** `v0.0.12`
**Purpose:** Implement semantic classification, Images/Videos, stream manifests, canonical URL/dedup projection and glob admission/exclude veto.
**Evidence:** ADR-0002, MATRIX-0005/0006.

STEP-07 fast-path result: added HTTP(S) canonical URL projection using platform serialization with only fragment removal and query preservation; bounded semantic classification into image/video/stream_manifest/audio/other/unknown using recognized MIME, image request-type fallback and allowlisted extensions; HLS/DASH recognition; full-canonical-URL case-sensitive glob v1 with `*`, `?` and explicit escapes only; default Images/Videos admission and `(preset OR include) AND NOT exclude` semantics; reversible Watch+document+canonical-URL occurrence grouping that retains every raw observation; and Watch-start filter preflight/rollback for invalid frozen globs. The IndexedDB physical schema remains unchanged and Packagizer execution remains STEP-08. Focused validation passed resources/Watch/observation TypeScript plus 35/35 directly relevant tests and the pre-documentation diff check. The fast-path publication policy was revised by explicit user instruction to resume one slim final ZIP Library upload per proper iteration without reintroducing pre-bundles, sidecars or cold/deterministic verification ceremony.

### STEP-08 - Packagizer Rules, Conditions, Templates, Tokens, and Derived Action Registry
**Target:** `v0.0.13`
**Purpose:** Implement ordered declarative rules, Missing-aware namespaced tokens, bounded safe transforms, atomic derived actions and stop-after-success behavior. Fresh research must bound the initial naming/grouping/action vocabulary without creating downloader control.
**Evidence:** ADR-0002, MATRIX-0007.

STEP-08 fast-path result: added frozen Watch-reference-ordered Packagizer rules with ANDed immutable-source conditions, Missing-aware namespaced tokens, bounded template parsing/transforms, atomic per-rule action application, successful-match stop behavior, and an explicit local-only derived action registry (`set_filename`, `set_group`, `set_comment`). Unknown/sensitive/derived-state tokens, regex, arbitrary code and downloader-control actions fail closed. Page/field token names are admitted but remain Missing until later exact-document PageField authority supplies values. Watch start now preflights frozen rule/template syntax and rolls back an invalid composed session. Fresh current JDownloader support/source research reconfirmed the ordered rule + dynamic-variable behavioral reference without expanding crsniffer into downloader semantics. Focused validation passed five strict TypeScript lanes and 58/58 directly dependent tests before documentation-only pointer updates.

### STEP-09 - Integrated Resource Evaluation, Preview/Explanation, and Immutable Projection
**Target:** `v0.0.14`
**Purpose:** Compose classification/admission/rules/templates into one pure evaluator used by live and Preview/Test with redacted structural explanations and durable admitted projections.
**Evidence:** ADR-0002, CONSTRAINT-0004, FINDING-0016.

STEP-09 fast-path result: composed STEP-07 classification/admission and STEP-08 Packagizer semantics into one pure `evaluateResourceCandidate` engine used identically by live observation finalization and Preview/Test. Added immutable admitted `ResourceProjection` snapshots with canonical URL, classification/admission facts, derived filename/group/comment metadata and frozen definition-set digest authority; rejected and semantic-failure outcomes remain projection-free and explicit. Durable explanations are bounded structural traces containing IDs, source-state/outcome markers, matched preset names and glob indexes, transform names, overwrite/rollback facts and error codes without raw token values, URL query secrets or rendered values. Raw `ResourceObservation.value` remains untouched; its optional evaluation sibling is attached on the single initial durable write, with no new object store or physical IndexedDB version. Structural evaluation-service failures fail closed before observation persistence and leave terminal pending state replayable with the same preassigned observation ID. Focused validation passed seven strict TypeScript lanes, 74/74 directly dependent tests, the pre-documentation diff check and static checks proving exact Preview/live delegation, unchanged IndexedDB topology and no new Chrome authority. Phase P2 is complete under the fast path.

## Phase P2 success criteria

- Explicit Watch can produce durable immutable observations and deterministic admitted projections.
- Permission loss, storage failure and evaluator failure are visible and fail closed.
- Preview and live semantics are identical for the same frozen input context.

# Phase P3 - Exact-Document Page Enrichment

### STEP-10 - Top-Level PageContext, Document Attribution, Navigation, and Same-Document Revision
**Target:** `v0.0.15`
**Purpose:** Implement top-level document identity, request attribution, webNavigation/history/fragment invalidation and fail-closed ambiguity handling.
**Evidence:** ADR-0003, MATRIX-0009.
**Result:** Complete under fast path. Browser-session PageContext uses exact Chrome `documentId` plus monotonic same-document `pageRevision`; Watch-scoped webNavigation reconstructs ancestry, hard commits replace the document boundary, History/fragment navigation advances revision, and observations freeze attribution at their first request event without later backfill. Required API permission becomes `storage + webRequest + webNavigation`; IndexedDB remains physical v1 with the same five stores. CSS/XPath/DOM mapping execution remains STEP-11.

### STEP-11 - CSS/XPath Field Mapping, Reads, Cardinality, Fallback, Transforms, and Validation
**Target:** `v0.0.16`
**Purpose:** Implement the typed mapping evaluator with exact-document scripting, snapshot/scalar behavior, safe reads/transforms and explicit failure semantics.
**Evidence:** ADR-0003, MATRIX-0008.
**Result:** Complete under fast path. Added strict closed-schema PageFieldMapping v1 validation, exact top-document `chrome.scripting.executeScript` in `ISOLATED` world, CSS static-node and typed XPath scalar/ordered-snapshot reads, explicit first/optional_one/exact_one/many cardinality, Missing-or-rejection-only fallback, bounded safe transforms/validation, and before/after PageContext revision checks. Required API permissions become `storage + webRequest + webNavigation + scripting`; IndexedDB remains physical v1 with the same five stores. PageFieldSnapshot persistence and `${page.*}`/`${field.*}` token integration remain STEP-12.

### STEP-12 - PageFieldSnapshot, Page/Field Tokens, Dependency Freeze, and Stale Rejection
**Target:** `v0.0.17`
**Purpose:** Integrate referenced frozen mappings into Watch evaluation, immutable PageFieldSnapshots and `${page.*}`/`${field.*}` tokens with Preview/live parity.
**Evidence:** ADR-0003, ADR-0002, MATRIX-0010.
**Result:** Complete under fast path. Watch preflight now resolves the exact enabled frozen `page.*`/`field.<slug>` dependency set and rejects missing mapping dependencies before activation. On-demand exact-document enrichment writes deterministic one-per-observation `PageFieldSnapshot` records containing Watch definition-set digest, top-document/pageRevision provenance, mapping ID/revision/digest authority, page URL/origin/title facts and typed field outcomes; stale/unattributed/revision-raced observations never read or substitute the current page. Preview uses the same snapshot builder and resource evaluator without persisting page-value history, while live evaluation persists and reuses the exact immutable snapshot. Resource evaluation/projection/explanation logical schemas advance to v2 to carry structural page-enrichment authority; existing persisted v1 evaluation siblings remain readable, IndexedDB remains physical v1 with the same five stores, and permissions remain `storage + webRequest + webNavigation + scripting`. Phase P3 is complete.

## Phase P3 success criteria

- Page enrichment never substitutes a later/current document for stale or ambiguous attribution.
- Page/field token values are reproducible from frozen mapping/document provenance.

