**Target:** `v0.0.18`
**Purpose:** Implement reconstructable Side Panel state, versioned messages, request freshness/latest-state reconciliation and service-worker/panel reconnect without local canonical authority.
**Evidence:** ADR-0004, ADR-0005.
**Result:** Complete under fast path. Added a bounded reconstructable Side Panel control plane using current core request/response envelopes for one-shot `panel.hydrate` and schema-v1 runtime Port invalidation hints. Hydration echoes a client request sequence and the panel discards stale out-of-order responses; it rehydrates on panel mount, active-tab change, Port invalidation, and Port reconnect. Ports carry only invalidation reasons, never canonical snapshots, and malformed or failed UI notifications cannot affect durable observation capture. Watch / Rules / Settings are now navigable shell destinations; Watch remains the only implemented domain workspace in STEP-13, while resource rows/virtualization remain STEP-14 and rule/settings editing remain STEP-15/16. Required permissions and IndexedDB v1/five-store topology are unchanged. Focused validation passed 46/46 across core messaging, Watch, observations, and control plane plus four strict TypeScript lanes and static bounded-hydration/authority checks.

