## Delivery governance

One ROADMAP-0003 step maps to one product version by default. STEP-01 is research/interaction-contract work and must not pull broad STEP-02+ UI implementation forward. STEP-02 through STEP-09 are bounded product-experience implementation steps. STEP-10 through STEP-12 are hardening steps over the feature-complete UI. STEP-13 and STEP-14 are release-boundary work and must use risk-appropriate/full recovery evidence.

Every UI step must inspect the then-latest promoted Crscraper UI/UX roadmap evidence when materially useful, but donor patterns remain read-only evidence. Current first-party Chrome/WAI/accessibility authority must be refreshed when a step depends on browser APIs, permission behavior, focus semantics, custom widgets, target sizing, reflow or assistive-technology expectations.

A donor pattern may be deliberately adapted or rejected. Crsniffer's domain/runtime differences are legitimate, but backend generality is not by itself a justification for exposing a poorer normal-user interaction.

