# Governance Helpers

These optional standard-library Python scripts automate mechanical repository governance tasks. They are not project authority and do not make Python the application language.

## Initialization manager

```bash
python3 agents/scripts/initialization-manager.py status
python3 agents/scripts/initialization-manager.py init --project my-project --version v0.1.0
python3 agents/scripts/initialization-manager.py validate
```

The initialization manager owns the one-time reusable-starter → project identity transition. It updates only structured/managed identity surfaces, resets starter-owned project history, preserves source provenance, and refuses a second initialization. It does not globally replace text or rename the workspace directory. See `agents/governance/initialization.md`.

## Record manager

```bash
python3 agents/scripts/record-manager.py validate
python3 agents/scripts/record-manager.py list
python3 agents/scripts/record-manager.py next-id roadmap
python3 agents/scripts/record-manager.py create finding "External Retry Contract" --provenance vXXXX
python3 agents/scripts/record-manager.py create deferral "Live Integration Verification" --environment --revisit-condition "authenticated integration environment is available" --provenance vXXXX
```

Use `--stdout` on `create` to preview a rendered artifact without writing it.

## Knowledge manager

```bash
python3 agents/scripts/knowledge-manager.py validate
python3 agents/scripts/knowledge-manager.py next-id
python3 agents/scripts/knowledge-manager.py create http "Retry Semantics" --source-kind official --provenance vXXXX
python3 agents/scripts/knowledge-manager.py stale
```

## Iteration manager

```bash
python3 agents/scripts/iteration-manager.py create <slug> v0.0.1 --base HEAD --summary "Bounded change"
python3 agents/scripts/iteration-manager.py changelog <slug> v0.0.1
python3 agents/scripts/iteration-manager.py seal <slug> v0.0.1 --result HEAD
python3 agents/scripts/iteration-manager.py validate
python3 agents/scripts/iteration-manager.py verify <slug> v0.0.1
```

The iteration manager owns the minimal `iterations/{slug}.vN.N.N/` ledger. Drafts contain `manifest.yaml` plus structured `change.md`; sealing adds a full-index binary-capable `changes.diff`. The manager renders root `CHANGELOG.md` deterministically from the latest 20 eligible `change.md` records, verifies that generated view is committed and synchronized before sealing, excludes `iterations/**` from the replayed workspace projection to avoid self-reference, and verifies the diff against an isolated Git index. It does not create commits, branches, tags, merges, or rebases. See `agents/governance/iteration.md`.

## Workspace manager

```bash
python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py audit
python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py snapshot --version vN.N.N
python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py bundle --version vN.N.N
python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py pre --version vN.N.N
python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py capture --kind checkpoint --version vN.N.N
python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py verify --version vN.N.N --pre
python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py verify --version vN.N.N --kind checkpoint --timestamp YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ
python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py verify --version vN.N.N
python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py cleanup --version vN.N.N --kind checkpoint --retain 3
python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py seal --version vN.N.N
python3 agents/scripts/workspace-manager.py seal --version vN.N.N --keep-pre
```

The workspace manager owns recoverable **workspace state**. By default it writes recovery artifacts under `/mnt/data`: `snapshots/{identity}/`, a deterministic ZIP, `.zip.sha256`, and `.snapshot.json`. The singleton `{project}.vN.N.N-pre` identity preserves the predecessor state for a target version; repeatable non-promoted captures use `{project}.vN.N.N-{kind}.YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ`. A successful promoted seal independently verifies its recovery set and then removes the matching verified `-pre` artifacts by default; `--keep-pre` preserves them. Timestamped captures are retained until explicit `cleanup` prunes a selected kind. The manager rejects symlinks, excludes transient tool state such as `.git`, caches, virtual environments, and `node_modules`, verifies archive safety/content/modes/checksum/metadata, cold-extracts for content equivalence, and reproduces the ZIP byte-for-byte. See `agents/governance/management.md` for command routing and `agents/governance/recovery.md` for policy.

## Authority boundary

Scripts may render, inspect, validate, snapshot, or bundle. They MUST NOT auto-accept an ADR, close a roadmap step, resolve a deferral, or claim an unavailable environment check passed.
