<file path="docs/troubleshooting.md">
# Troubleshooting

Use the Side Panel **Settings → Diagnostics & support** summary before reaching for internal identifiers. It reports runtime health, migration state, schema versions and bounded record counts; the expanded technical disclosure remains structural/redacted and intentionally excludes URLs, request/document IDs, headers, cookies, bodies, credentials and token values.

If capture is degraded, stop Watch before using destructive Clear. **Clear history** preserves saved definitions/preferences; **Clear all local data** also resets them and restores only Default Watch. Neither operation revokes Chrome-granted optional site access. If a Clear operation reports an error, do not assume every scope completed; preserve the prior portable bundle as rollback/recovery evidence and inspect diagnostics before further destructive action.

At v0.0.28, an observation write/quota failure ends the active Watch with a storage-failure explanation rather than continuing to claim successful capture. If the browser session is still alive, the terminal pending trace is retained for service-worker retry once storage recovers. Reloading/restarting the browser clears session coordination and never auto-resumes Watch. Settings storage estimates are approximate: warning/critical state can run the configured terminal-history retention policy early, but it does not authorize deletion of in-policy canonical history. If pressure remains critical after retention, use the explicit Clear controls or free browser/device storage; do not assume Crsniffer silently pruned more data.

## Appearance and Chrome themes

Crsniffer follows public light/dark/system-color behavior rather than a hard-coded color palette. If the Side Panel looks different from Chrome's toolbar when a custom Chrome theme is installed, that can be expected: extension pages do not receive Chrome's private toolbar/WebUI theme-token palette. Crsniffer still follows light/dark, native control accent, selection and forced/high-contrast behavior. Do not treat a custom-theme hue mismatch as a permission or rendering failure.
</file>

