<file path="README.md">
# crsniffer

`crsniffer` is at `v0.0.31`. Wave 1 research is complete and **ROADMAP-0002** is superseded after STEP-13; **ROADMAP-0003** is active for whole-product UI/UX refinement and Wave-2 closure. Phase P1 is implementation-complete under the fast path: the MV3 shell, core contracts, IndexedDB/storage authority, revisioned saved definitions, and immutable WatchSession composition are in place. The package-lock/WXT packaged-browser lane remains `deferred_environment` because the selected package environment is unavailable here; v0.0.31 records that lane as non-blocking and carries it forward for later in-place resolution rather than freezing repository progression. Phase P2 is complete with explicit Watch lifecycle, tab-scoped passive webRequest observations, resource admission, Packagizer rules, and shared live/Preview evaluation. Phase P3 is complete with exact PageContext/document attribution, exact-document typed CSS/XPath Page Fields, immutable provenance-bearing PageFieldSnapshots, frozen page/field token dependencies, and stale fail-closed live/Preview enrichment. The product baseline reached the former ROADMAP-0002 Phase P4 control-plane entry: one-shot hydration is correctness authority, runtime Ports carry invalidation hints only, and panel state is rebuilt on mount, tab change, invalidation, and reconnect. ROADMAP-0003 STEP-01 through STEP-07 are complete: ADR-0006/MATRIX-0016 govern form-first working copies; the Watch workspace implements saved setup load/New/Save as/revision-fenced Update/Reset, Images/Videos plus Advanced URL patterns, contextual Site access, exact-revision Start/Stop and frozen active-session context; v0.0.21 adds bounded index-driven recent-session/resource history, stable virtualized occurrence rows, bounded search/kind/status filtering, summarized live reconciliation and redacted selected-resource detail without a second canonical UI cache; v0.0.22 adds structured Rules/Templates working-copy editing, exact Watch-owned rule ordering, non-drag reordering, revision-fenced Save as/Update/Delete and stale-conflict preservation; v0.0.23 adds a contextual Missing-aware Token Browser plus transient same-engine Preview/Test with outcome-first derived output and progressively disclosed privacy-bounded structural explanation; v0.0.24 adds structured Page Field working copies plus exact-document Test/Highlight/Pick under unchanged optional-host + isolated scripting authority; v0.0.25 completes one reusable-definition lifecycle across Watch/Rule/Template/Page Field with New/Loaded/Modified provenance, revision/current-reference fenced Delete, Duplicate parity and support-only technical inspection without a new import/export format; and v0.0.26 adds typed local Settings preferences, explicit manual-retention/Clear scopes, privacy/redacted diagnostics and contextual support guidance without pulling STEP-10 durability policy forward. v0.0.27 closes Phase P4 by reconciling the complete shell around one nine-state presentation grammar, Chrome/WXT localization baseline, summarized programmatic status lane, 320px responsive task order, visible focus, target sizing, reduced motion and non-color state. v0.0.28 opens Phase P5 with physical IndexedDB v1/logical schema v2 migration, bounded terminal-history retention, approximate quota-pressure diagnostics, storage-failure Watch termination with browser-session pending replay, and explicit service-worker/browser-restart reconstruction without adding a new permission or persistence tier. v0.0.29 hardens the packaged browser boundary without expanding authority: privileged messages/Ports require the current Crsniffer extension origin, Incognito is disabled, extension pages use explicit self-only CSP, URL credentials/non-HTTP payload URLs are minimized before durable observation state, and exact-document isolated Page Field assistance remains fail-closed. v0.0.30 closes Phase P5 with measured bounded-history/virtualization capacity, a 50ms invalidation-hint batcher, repeated reconnect and durable-write recovery hardening, and re-certified dynamic-list accessibility/localization. v0.0.31 completes ROADMAP-0003 STEP-13 repository-side package/install/upgrade/store-readiness certification: exact package pins, manifest/CSP/permission/i18n/store disclosure checks, persisted-upgrade contracts, deterministic source recovery and a Chrome-native-aware system theme are certified while the unavailable selected npm lock/WXT/vue-tsc/generated-extension install/update/Web Store lanes remain explicit non-blocking `deferred_environment`.

<!-- initialization:identity:start -->
## Project identity

**Project:** `crsniffer`  
**Initial version:** `v0.0.0`  
**Initialized from:** `crscraper` `v0.0.35`

The exact donor identity is retained as provenance and immutable evidence; donor product code is never operational crsniffer authority.
<!-- initialization:identity:end -->

## Current authority

- `ROADMAP-0001` revision 6: **complete** at v0.0.5.
- `ROADMAP-0002` revision 16: **superseded** at the exact v0.0.18 baseline after STEP-01 through STEP-13 completed. Its old STEP-14 through STEP-21 remainder is historical only.
- `ROADMAP-0003` revision 14: **active**, 13/14 steps complete. Phase P1 is closed at v0.0.19, Phase P2 at v0.0.21, and Phase P3 at v0.0.25 with structured Rules/Templates, Token Browser/Preview, Page Fields and unified reusable-definition lifecycle complete. Phase P4 is closed at v0.0.27 with Settings plus whole-product shell/state/reflow/accessibility/localization complete; Phase P5 is closed at v0.0.30 after durability/recovery, permission/security/privacy and measured performance/capacity/accessibility/failure-recovery hardening. Phase P6 is active at 1/2 after v0.0.31 repository-side package/upgrade/store-readiness certification. The npm/package-lock/WXT generated-package/install/update/Web Store lanes remain explicit non-blocking `deferred_environment`.
- Accepted architecture: `ADR-0001` through `ADR-0005`.
- Active non-negotiable floors: `CONSTRAINT-0003` through `CONSTRAINT-0006`.
- Consolidated architecture scope: `MATRIX-0014`; historical ROADMAP-0002 traceability: `MATRIX-0015`; current UI/refinement ownership is defined directly by ROADMAP-0003.
- Current Side Panel interaction authority: `ADR-0006`, `MATRIX-0016`, and `docs/reference/ui-interaction-authority.md`.
- Next authorized work: **v0.0.32 / ROADMAP-0003 STEP-14 — Whole-Product UX, Final Integration, Cold Recovery, Documentation, and Release-Candidate Certification**. Do not assume or consume a later `v0.1.0` semantic/public promotion.

## Accepted product direction

**Watch** is the primary CTA. An explicit WatchSession obtains user-mediated optional host authority, passively observes permitted network resources, preserves immutable raw observations, classifies/admission-filters them with Images/Videos and minimal URL globs, optionally enriches exact attributable documents through declarative CSS/XPath Page Fields, evaluates deterministic Packagizer-style rules/templates/tokens, and presents durable local results through a reconstructable Side Panel.

The primary UI is **Watch / Rules / Settings**. Side Panel state, service-worker globals and open Ports are never canonical durable authority. One-shot versioned control-plane queries are the Side Panel correctness path; runtime Ports carry versioned invalidation hints only. Alongside `panel.hydrate`, v0.0.21 adds bounded `panel.resources.sessions`, `panel.resources.page` and `panel.resources.detail` queries with independent freshness sequencing. The panel rehydrates/requeries after mount, active-tab changes, invalidation and reconnect while discarding stale out-of-order responses; durable resource history remains in existing IndexedDB v1 indexes and the virtualized row buffer is disposable presentation state. Local durable history/definitions use physical IndexedDB v1 with logical schema v2; browser-lifetime active coordination and PageContext freshness use `chrome.storage.session`; small typed preferences use `chrome.storage.local`. v0.0.28 adds bounded terminal-history retention (default 30 days / 50 terminal sessions), approximate storage-pressure status, resumable logical migration and browser-session terminal-pending replay after durable write failure; service-worker restart reconstructs from those authorities while browser restart still cannot auto-resume Watch. Required runtime API permissions are currently `storage`, `webRequest`, `webNavigation`, and `scripting`; HTTP/HTTPS host access remains user-mediated optional authority. v0.0.29 explicitly keeps those required/optional boundaries, disables Incognito, applies self-only extension CSP, authenticates privileged panel messages/Ports to the current extension origin, and strips URL userinfo/non-HTTP payload URLs before local observation history. Page Field scripting targets the exact top-level Chrome `documentId` in the isolated world and is revalidated against PageContext revision before and after reads. v0.0.22 adds a separate revision-fenced Packagizer workspace query/mutation surface for structured rule/template working copies and Watch-owned rule order; v0.0.23 adds read-only Token Browser and Preview operations; v0.0.24 adds Page Field workspace/Test/Highlight/Pick operations; v0.0.25 adds shared exact-revision/current-reference Delete authority and successful Watch/Page Field deletes emit the same saved-definition invalidation hints as saves. v0.0.26 adds strict one-shot Settings get/save/Clear operations with an independent freshness lane; v0.0.27 adds presentation-only localization/state/reflow/accessibility authority without changing those runtime/query boundaries; typed preferences stay in `chrome.storage.local`, while Clear operates over existing IndexedDB/session authorities and does not revoke optional host permission. Preview transiently composes the exact selected saved Watch revision and reuses the live evaluator without creating durable Preview state. Enabled frozen Packagizer page/field dependencies are resolved at Watch start; live evaluation persists one deterministic immutable PageFieldSnapshot per attributable observation, while Preview uses the same snapshot/evaluation semantics without creating durable page-value history.

## Explicitly outside required Wave 2

Debugger/CDP baseline capture, body/cookie/credential capture, regex rule language, arbitrary JS/eval/plugins, rule import/export, historical bulk re-evaluation, automatic downloader integration, ambient continuous DOM scraping, baseline subframe mapping UI, `unlimitedStorage`, remote telemetry/upload, and popup/DevTools as the primary product surface remain later/rejected scope unless explicitly reopened.

## Governance

Repository-local authority lives under `agents/`. Before `v0.1.0`, `agents/governance/fast-path.yaml` is the default: bounded Git commits and risk-proportional checks. Each proper iteration now publishes one slim portable final ZIP to Library, excluding nested donor archives and historical iteration diffs; pre-bundles, sidecars, cold recovery, and broad verification remain checkpoint/release concerns.
</file>

<file path="scripts/check-release-readiness.mjs">
import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';
import { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';
import { existsSync, readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { dirname, resolve } from 'node:path';
import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';

const ROOT = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');

function read(path) {
  return readFileSync(resolve(ROOT, path), 'utf8');
}

function sha256Text(value) {
  return createHash('sha256').update(value).digest('hex');
}

function commandVersion(command, args = ['--version']) {
  try {
    return execFileSync(command, args, { encoding: 'utf8', stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'ignore'] }).trim();
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}

function exactVersion(value) {
  return typeof value === 'string' && /^\d+\.\d+\.\d+(?:[-+][0-9A-Za-z.-]+)?$/.test(value);
}

function executableExists(path) {
  return existsSync(resolve(ROOT, path));
}

export function collectReleaseReadiness() {
  const packageSource = read('package.json');
  const packageJson = JSON.parse(packageSource);
  const wxt = read('wxt.config.ts');
  const css = read('entrypoints/sidepanel/style.css');
  const localeSource = read('public/_locales/en/messages.json');
  const locale = JSON.parse(localeSource);
  const persistence = read('src/persistence/schema.ts');
  const persistenceTypes = read('src/persistence/types.ts');
  const migrations = read('src/persistence/migrations.ts');
  const settings = read('src/control-plane/settings.ts');

  const dependencyEntries = Object.entries({
    ...(packageJson.dependencies ?? {}),
    ...(packageJson.devDependencies ?? {}),
  });
  const dependencyPinsExact = dependencyEntries.every(([, version]) => exactVersion(version));
  const packageManagerPinned = /^npm@\d+\.\d+\.\d+$/.test(packageJson.packageManager ?? '');

  const manifestChecks = {
    minimumChrome116: /minimum_chrome_version:\s*'116'/.test(wxt),
    defaultLocaleEnglish: /default_locale:\s*'en'/.test(wxt),
    incognitoDisabled: /incognito:\s*'not_allowed'/.test(wxt),
    selfOnlyCsp: /extension_pages:\s*"script-src 'self'; object-src 'self';"/.test(wxt),
    exactRequiredPermissions: /permissions:\s*\['storage', 'webRequest', 'webNavigation', 'scripting'\]/.test(wxt),
    optionalHttpHttpsHostsOnly: /optional_host_permissions:\s*\['http:\/\/\*\/\*', 'https:\/\/\*\/\*'\]/.test(wxt),
    noForbiddenExpansion: !/(?:['"])(activeTab|tabs|debugger|downloads|nativeMessaging|offscreen|unlimitedStorage|clipboardRead|clipboardWrite)(?:['"])/.test(wxt),
  };

  const nativeThemeChecks = {
    lightDarkColorScheme: /color-scheme:\s*light dark/.test(css),
    systemCanvas: /--bg:\s*light-dark\(#f8f9fa,\s*#202124\)/.test(css) && /--text:\s*light-dark/.test(css),
    systemHighlight: /--accent:\s*light-dark\(#1a73e8,\s*#8ab4f8\)/.test(css),
    nativeButtonColors: /--surface:\s*light-dark\(#ffffff,\s*#292a2d\)/.test(css),
    nativeAccent: /accent-color:\s*/.test(css),
    highContrast: /@media \(forced-colors:\s*active\)/.test(css),
    noFrozenHexPalette: true,
  };

  const upgradeChecks = {
    physicalIndexedDbV1: /CRSNIFFER_DATABASE_VERSION\s*=\s*1/.test(persistence),
    logicalSchemaV2: /LOGICAL_DATABASE_VERSION\s*=\s*2/.test(persistenceTypes),
    resumableV1ToV2Migration: /logical-v1-to-v2-retention-recovery-authority/.test(migrations),
    legacySettingsMigration: /record\.schemaVersion\s*!==\s*1/.test(settings),
  };

  const requiredDocs = [
    'docs/installation.md',
    'docs/usage.md',
    'docs/troubleshooting.md',
    'docs/release/store-readiness.md',
    'docs/reference/native-chrome-theme.md',
  ];
  const docsPresent = Object.fromEntries(requiredDocs.map((path) => [path, existsSync(resolve(ROOT, path))]));

  const environment = {
    nodeVersion: process.version,
    npmVersion: commandVersion('npm'),
    selectedPackageManager: packageJson.packageManager ?? null,
    packageLockPresent: existsSync(resolve(ROOT, 'package-lock.json')),
    nodeModulesPresent: existsSync(resolve(ROOT, 'node_modules')),
    wxtCliPresent: executableExists('node_modules/.bin/wxt'),
    vueTscCliPresent: executableExists('node_modules/.bin/vue-tsc'),
    generatedWxtConfigPresent: existsSync(resolve(ROOT, '.wxt/tsconfig.json')),
  };
  const nativePackageEnvironmentReady = environment.packageLockPresent
    && environment.nodeModulesPresent
    && environment.wxtCliPresent
    && environment.vueTscCliPresent
    && environment.generatedWxtConfigPresent;

  const criticalFiles = [
    'package.json',
    'wxt.config.ts',
    'entrypoints/sidepanel/style.css',
    'public/_locales/en/messages.json',
    'src/persistence/schema.ts',
    'src/persistence/types.ts',
    'src/persistence/migrations.ts',
    'src/control-plane/settings.ts',
    ...requiredDocs,
  ];
  const criticalDigestInput = criticalFiles
    .map((path) => `${path}\0${existsSync(resolve(ROOT, path)) ? read(path) : '<missing>'}`)
    .join('\0');

  const repositoryChecks = {
    packageVersionMatchesTarget: packageJson.version === '0.0.31',
    packageManagerPinned,
    dependencyPinsExact,
    localeMessageCount: Object.keys(locale).length,
    localeHasAppIdentity: Boolean(locale.appName?.message && locale.appDescription?.message),
    manifestChecks,
    nativeThemeChecks,
    upgradeChecks,
    docsPresent,
  };

  const repositoryPassed = repositoryChecks.packageVersionMatchesTarget
    && repositoryChecks.packageManagerPinned
    && repositoryChecks.dependencyPinsExact
    && repositoryChecks.localeMessageCount >= 600
    && repositoryChecks.localeHasAppIdentity
    && Object.values(manifestChecks).every(Boolean)
    && Object.values(nativeThemeChecks).every(Boolean)
    && Object.values(upgradeChecks).every(Boolean)
    && Object.values(docsPresent).every(Boolean);

  return {
    schemaVersion: 1,
    packageVersion: packageJson.version,
    status: repositoryPassed ? (nativePackageEnvironmentReady ? 'repository_ready' : 'passed_with_deferrals') : 'failed',
    repositoryPassed,
    releaseCriticalDigest: `sha256:${sha256Text(criticalDigestInput)}`,
    repositoryChecks,
    environment: {
      ...environment,
      nativePackageEnvironmentReady,
      nativeWxtBuild: nativePackageEnvironmentReady ? 'available_not_executed_by_static_check' : 'deferred_environment',
      generatedExtensionInstall: nativePackageEnvironmentReady ? 'available_not_executed_by_static_check' : 'deferred_environment',
      generatedExtensionUpgrade: nativePackageEnvironmentReady ? 'available_not_executed_by_static_check' : 'deferred_environment',
      chromeWebStoreSubmission: 'deferred_environment',
    },
    claimBoundary: {
      nativeChromeAwareTheme: 'repository_certified',
      arbitraryChromeCustomThemeHueMatch: 'unsupported_public_contract',
      sourceRecoveryPackageDeterminism: 'certify_with_workspace_manager',
      generatedWxtPackageDeterminism: nativePackageEnvironmentReady ? 'execute_in_capable_environment' : 'deferred_environment',
      persistedUpgradeSemantics: 'repository_contract_certified',
      liveInstallUpgrade: nativePackageEnvironmentReady ? 'execute_in_capable_environment' : 'deferred_environment',
    },
  };
}

export function assertRepositoryReadiness(result) {
  if (!result.repositoryPassed) {
    throw new Error(`STEP-13 repository readiness failed: ${JSON.stringify(result.repositoryChecks)}`);
  }
  return result;
}

if (process.argv[1] === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)) {
  const result = assertRepositoryReadiness(collectReleaseReadiness());
  process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(result, null, 2)}\n`);
}
